Ask the design session for a decision on resume at 17: today a relaunch goes to Home. Also mention the chip \"mm\".\n   - Propose a follow-up session (\"own_initiative\") for the v1 import dropping printers whose vendor isn't loaded, with Kenneth's Qidi copy as evidence. Optionally also propose follow-ups for the Home drop-zone line naming the first card, and for import progress feedback.\n   - The merge-and-push question to Kenneth from before is still open.\n   - Mention to Kenneth: Deny any lingering keychain prompt.\n   - Clean-up: the dev server (`python3 server.py` on 8767, background task bh9aencr4) is still running. The test app is killed.\n   - Update the task list (steps 3–6 are still open) and call `mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up`.\n\n8. **Current Work:**\n   I had just committed d606562b06 on `claude/first-run-printer-step`:\n   > \"OrcaSlicer import: install each saved printer's base profile first, and keep the selection on Retry\"\n\n   That followed `jusprin_tests`: \"All tests passed (1002 assertions in 165 test cases)\", and \"[orca_import]\" 74 assertions in 5 test cases. Every in-app path run is finished; the last was J with a file opened, which passed.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step:**\n   Stop the dev server. Mark the task list's remaining steps done. Call `mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up` with a recap that starts with commit d606562b06, then give the per-path report the design session asked for:\n   > \"Report back which paths you saw pass in the built app.\"\n\n   In the report:\n   - Ask \"Decision needed\" about resuming on 17, one question.\n   - Propose the v1-import vendor bug as its own session with `start_session` \"own_initiative\".\n   - Keep the merge question to Kenneth open; don't merge or push.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin--claude-worktrees-first-run-flow-f7be35/c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]}}
