{"parentUuid":"ebe1661a-7b06-45e6-a89f-35e0cf86aab5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d97ef8e1-febe-4fa1-82dd-c20e66105c0f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011XbTLxCbZD4aEVozRQAML9","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"message\":\"Successfully stopped task: bh9aencr4 (exec python3 server.py)\",\"task_id\":\"bh9aencr4\",\"task_type\":\"local_bash\",\"command\":\"exec python3 server.py\"}"}]},"uuid":"9b200e90-9dae-4682-9d14-de19f27504f6","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:10:08.238Z","toolUseResult":{"message":"Successfully stopped task: bh9aencr4 (exec python3 server.py)","task_id":"bh9aencr4","task_type":"local_bash","command":"exec python3 server.py"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ebe1661a-7b06-45e6-a89f-35e0cf86aab5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-printer-step","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"9b200e90-9dae-4682-9d14-de19f27504f6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkhmQ3jKWwCj21sVfMpP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H5uVpARWFYWQomT1BkFQeL","name":"mcp__ccd_session__start_session","input":{"initiation":"own_initiative","title":"v1 import drops printers whose vendor isn't loaded","context":"fresh","prompt":"When JusPrin imports a JusPrin v1 data folder, v1 printer presets whose `inherits` names a base profile from a vendor that isn't installed yet get dropped without any message. The cause is that JusPrin loads a vendor's system presets only once one of that vendor's printers is installed. Reproduce it with a copy of Kenneth's real v1 `user/` folder. Copy it from `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin/user` into a scratch folder; that original folder is read-only, so never modify it and don't copy its conf. Point `JUSPRIN_V1_DATADIR` at the copy and use a fresh `--datadir`. Expected result: \"Qidi X-Plus 4 0.4 nozzle - Copy\" is missing from Home, while \"MyKlipper 0.4 nozzle - Copy\" and \"Untitled\" show up. The fix should follow commit d606562b06 on `claude/first-run-printer-step`, which fixed the same problem for the OrcaSlicer import. In `import_orca_files` (`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`), that commit installs each base listed by `orca_printer_bases(files)` through `SetupCommands::install_and_select_printer` before it imports. Reuse that helper for the v1 path in `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/V1Import.cpp` (or wherever the v1 user presets get copied in) rather than writing a second one. Done means: you reproduce the drop in the built app, the fix lands with a unit test in `tests/jusprin/`, and the Qidi copy shows up on Home after a fresh v1 import.","background":"JusPrin is a fork of OrcaSlicer. On first launch it can import a v1 JusPrin install, and this happens only when the datadir has no JusPrin2.conf. The import writes `jusprin/v1-import.json`. The OrcaSlicer import (onboarding board 07) used to fail the same way: a saved printer copy was reported \"its base profile isn't in JusPrin\". Commit d606562b06 fixed that by installing each saved printer's base profile first. The v1 path still has the bug, and there it fails silently because a user preset with an unloaded base is dropped at startup. Read `AGENTS.md` and `agent-docs/jusprin/fork-stewardship.md` before you touch any OrcaSlicer-owned file. When you build, use `-j4`, and check `uptime` and `pgrep ninja` first."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18139,"cache_read_input_tokens":106756,"output_tokens":1058,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18139,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1058,"cache_read_input_tokens":106756,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18139,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18139},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01H5uVpARWFYWQomT1BkFQeL":{"initiation":"own_initiative","title":"v1 import drops printers whose vendor isn't loaded","context":"fresh","prompt":"When JusPrin imports a JusPrin v1 data folder, v1 printer presets whose `inherits` names a base profile from a vendor that isn't installed yet get dropped without any message. The cause is that JusPrin loads a vendor's system presets only once one of that vendor's printers is installed. Reproduce it with a copy of Kenneth's real v1 `user/` folder. Copy it from `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin/user` into a scratch folder; that original folder is read-only, so never modify it and don't copy its conf. Point `JUSPRIN_V1_DATADIR` at the copy and use a fresh `--datadir`. Expected result: \"Qidi X-Plus 4 0.4 nozzle - Copy\" is missing from Home, while \"MyKlipper 0.4 nozzle - Copy\" and \"Untitled\" show up. The fix should follow commit d606562b06 on `claude/first-run-printer-step`, which fixed the same problem for the OrcaSlicer import. In `import_orca_files` (`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`), that commit installs each base listed by `orca_printer_bases(files)` through `SetupCommands::install_and_select_printer` before it imports. Reuse that helper for the v1 path in `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/V1Import.cpp` (or wherever the v1 user presets get copied in) rather than writing a second one. Done means: you reproduce the drop in the built app, the fix lands with a unit test in `tests/jusprin/`, and the Qidi copy shows up on Home after a fresh v1 import.","background":"JusPrin is a fork of OrcaSlicer. On first launch it can import a v1 JusPrin install, and this happens only when the datadir has no JusPrin2.conf. The import writes `jusprin/v1-import.json`. The OrcaSlicer import (onboarding board 07) used to fail the same way: a saved printer copy was reported \"its base profile isn't in JusPrin\". Commit d606562b06 fixed that by installing each saved printer's base profile first. The v1 path still has the bug, and there it fails silently because a user preset with an unloaded base is dropped at startup. Read `AGENTS.md` and `agent-docs/jusprin/fork-stewardship.md` before you touch any OrcaSlicer-owned file. When you build, use `-j4`, and check `uptime` and `pgrep ninja` first."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgkhmPpqaWLkjzq8jdR3u","requestRef":"d01d08a5-a7c3-4378-80a5-757611f73972","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ca690a97-bcdc-4775-816e-5c8cfa8e1cab","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:10:16.805Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType"