{"parentUuid":"aa1acb19-e539-4df0-b429-ab66b93f9933","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkhoASUGWrs98ST4dift","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_read_input_tokens":126172,"output_tokens":1338,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":68},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":454,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1338,"cache_read_input_tokens":126172,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":454},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7364,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgkhoA2AgqV1v5x2bMFcX","requestRef":"0bd6a545-8383-4286-a343-39309fe29ec1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"5a2138f6-aa74-4b1d-88b0-e2a2bb00988b","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:10:33.795Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-printer-step","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"5a2138f6-aa74-4b1d-88b0-e2a2bb00988b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkhoASUGWrs98ST4dift","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Commit d606562b06 on `claude/first-run-printer-step` fixes the OrcaSlicer import. Before it, every saved printer copy failed on a fresh install with \"its base profile isn't in JusPrin\". The cause: JusPrin loads a brand's built-in profiles only after one of that brand's printers is installed, and on a fresh install none is. The import now installs each saved printer's base profile first. The commit also fixes a second bug: pressing Retry on the import result used to switch the selected printer to whichever copy it had just brought in. Now the selection stays where it was. Unit tests pass (1002 assertions). Nothing is merged or pushed.\n\n**Why Kenneth got the manual form.** He launched with `--datadir ~/JusPrinStagingTest`. That makes JusPrin look for an OrcaSlicer folder at `~/OrcaSlicer`, which doesn't exist. I worked this out from the code and his launch command; his log is gone, so it's unverified. A normal install finds the folder.\n\n**Which account folder gets picked.** With no account recorded in OrcaSlicer's settings, JusPrin picks the account whose printer file was saved most recently. On Kenneth's Mac that is 51a48320.\n\n**Seen working in the built app, using a copy of Kenneth's real OrcaSlicer folder:**\n- **OrcaSlicer import:** 8 printers listed, all 8 imported, 3 filaments, the P1S selected, and a part sliced on it in about 29 min. The import freezes the screen for about 20 s with no progress shown.\n- **Import of a folder with only ticked printers:** works.\n- **Start fresh, then Back:** returns to the import screen.\n- **Manual printer form:** Continue adds the printer with its default plate and filament.\n- **\"Ask the agent\":** shows only for a signed-in user with credits, is hidden after \"Just slice for now\", and opens the printer chat. If you leave that chat with Back, Home shows no printer at all, only \"+ Add printer\".\n- **\"No printer yet\" card:** works, and adding a real printer replaces it.\n- **Import that brings no printer:** goes to the manual form.\n- **Quitting and relaunching:** works on the import screen and the manual form.\n- **Skipping the printer step:** a v1 import or a file opened during the welcome skips it.\n\n**Covered only by tests:**\n- What happens after you pick a folder with \"Choose the folder…\". The macOS folder dialog runs in a separate process that background control refuses to drive, and driving it would have meant taking over Kenneth's screen.\n- The Retry fix. In the real-folder run everything imported, so there was nothing to retry.\n\n**Found, not fixed:**\n- **v1 import drops printers:** it silently drops printers whose brand isn't loaded yet. With a copy of Kenneth's v1 folder, \"Qidi X-Plus 4 0.4 nozzle - Copy\" never shows up. It's the same cause as the OrcaSlicer bug, in older code. I tried to propose it as its own task, but the app refused because this session is on Remote Control. Tell me if you want me to start it.\n- **Home drop-zone line:** names the first printer card, not the selected printer. This predates this branch.\n- **Nozzle chip:** still reads \"0.4\" with no \"mm\".\n\nDecision needed: if someone quits on the screen that lists what the import brought in, a relaunch today goes to Home with onboarding marked finished. That's because the import result is kept only in memory. The spec says a relaunch resumes on the same screen. Keeping the result across a relaunch means saving it to disk, which is a small change. Leaving it as is costs nothing, and the person still lands on Home with everything imported. I'd lean toward leaving it, since that screen is only a summary. Should a relaunch come back to that screen?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_read_input_tokens":126172,"output_tokens":1338,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":68},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":454,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1338,"cache_read_input_tokens":126172,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":454},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgkhoA2AgqV1v5x2bMFcX","requestRef":"0bd6a545-8383-4286-a343-39309fe29ec1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"42d29102-0083-4166-9b9f-62c52e277110","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:10:39.133Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-printer-step","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
