"entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-printer-step","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"be5d640d-3f38-4392-acce-16ff509fcb6b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4fcc31c2-3e80-420b-a5c6-f7cbf63689ec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GwwP4GdALBWR1WpovBaQbh","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: first-run-flow-boards\ndescription: \"First-launch boards on the canvas onboarding page: variants A/B withdrawn 2026-11-02; Kenneth's one split welcome screen drawn as first-run-welcome-01..03 (version 87; no chrome + corner lockup in 88; the flow 04-11 in 89); builder build_first_run_page.py.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438\n  modified: 2026-11-03T03:48:37.053Z\n---\n\n2026-11-02: the no-wizard variants A and B (`first-run-a-*`, `first-run-b-*`) were withdrawn at Kenneth's request and removed in canvas version 87. Nothing else on the page had moved for them. In their place, `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1`, `-02-clip-final-frame` and `-03-clip-storyboard` draw the welcome screen from [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]]. Version 88 made it a full-window screen with no shell header or footer and the JusPrin lockup in the top-left corner (43 px tall, space-24/space-16), Kenneth's \"Lockup\" choice. They are built by `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`.\n\nGaps at the time: the type scale has no display size for the clip's big settings (page-title is used); there are no boards after \"Just slice for now\"; and nothing on the canvas now shows the \"assumed\" printer chip.\n\nFacts from the variant work that still apply: `printer_from_file` (`!is_named_printer`) would label an assumed default \"from the file\"; an empty data folder has no printers; the project chat can't add a printer; Home has no agent pane.\n\n**Why:** later sessions may find references to A/B and assume they are current.\n\n**How to apply:** treat A/B as history. Build the first launch from the welcome boards and the decision memory. Related: [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]], [[credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages]].\n\n**2026-11-03, version 93 (1793744174-5990), canvas ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ:** the boards now draw the built sign-in door. 01/02: Continue with Google, \"or\", email field + Continue with email, Terms line; 04: the browser-wait card (\"Nothing happened? Open the browser again\", \"Use an email code instead\"); 05: \"Signed in as alex@example.com · 500 credits\"; 10: Home's \"Set up the agent\" with the same door. New row y 7100: 12 email choice (Email me a 6-digit code, or password + Sign in), 13 wrong password, 14 typing the code, 15 wrong code, 16 code no longer works. Rows 07-08 and 09-10 and the superseded wizard moved down 940. The free doors dim only once signed in. Work copy `figma-mirror/work-first-run-door/`. Home's narrow column truncates the email field placeholder (\"you@exar\") — the app has the same CSS, so it likely looks the same there.\n---\nname: render-canvas-boards-with-render-dc\ndescription: \"figma-mirror/tools/composer/render_dc.py renders canvas boards to PNG through the canvas's own runtime, so dc-imports draw; render.py leaves them blank. Needs a work dir holding the live files and runtime/.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 3eabf4a3-87b6-4471-a4e5-b6fb9c14763a\n  modified: 2026-11-02T03:18:24.462Z\n---\n\n`python3 figma-mirror/tools/composer/render_dc.py <work dir> <out dir> [--dark] <board.dc.html>...` serves `<work>/project`, maps `support.js` to `<work>/runtime/dc-runtime.js` (the artifact's `artifact-type/dc-runtime.js`) and `/_blob/<id>` through `<work>/runtime/blobs.json`, and shoots headless Chrome at 2x with its own `--user-data-dir`. 21 boards take about 22 s. `--dark` flips the board's theme prop. A working `work-credits/` exists from the 2026-11-01 credits page.\n\nAlso learned drawing that page: anything absolutely placed over the Prepare screen needs a z-index above the composer band's, or the band paints over it. `figma-mirror/published/canvas` is stale (old board names), so pull live files with Artifact read `paths` + `out_dir` rather than copying from it. Related: [[canvas-boards-from-bundle-rules]], [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]].\n---\nname: design-source-is-claude-artifacts\ndescription: \"2026-10-20: Figma is retired for JusPrin design; the Claude Design System and JusPrin v2 canvas artifacts are the source of truth. Don't propose Figma changes or cite Figma.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 1ad40aa6-b204-449c-8be8-7600964a4f52\n  modified: 2026-10-27T20:28:20.888Z\n---\n\nKenneth, 2026-10-20: \"We're not changing Figma anymore. We have migrated to\nCloud artifact.\" The two Claude artifacts are now the design source of truth:\nthe Design System (https://claude.ai/artifact/3zgiix8rAw3rXextQnR5UL) and the\n\"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v). They\nstarted as copies of Figma ([[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]]), but\nthey are no longer re-synced from it.\n\n**Why:** design changes now happen in the artifacts, so a Figma-based argument\nor a \"change Figma\" proposal points at a dead file.\n\n**How to apply:** check designs by reading the artifact files (Artifact read\nwith `path`, e.g. `project/<page>-<frame>.dc.html` on the canvas); never\nsuggest editing Figma or waiting for Figma seat allowance; when citing a\ndesign, name the artifact board, not a Figma node. Describe what the board\nactually draws, not what a component's internal properties imply: a menu row\nwith no fill or border draws no shape at all, so it is not \"a square row\".\nOlder memories that say \"Figma is the source of truth\"\n([[design-token-sync-decisions]], [[figma-jusprin-v2-file]]) are superseded on\nthat point.\n\n**Restated by Kenneth later on 2026-10-20:** \"from now on, we should assume claude design artifact is the up to date design. figma is out of date.\" Docs changed the same day (uncommitted on jusprin-newui): agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md no longer points at Figma, and the repo skill .claude/skills/figma-agent-design is marked retired.\n\n**Also frozen (Kenneth, 2026-10-27):** the old Claude Design project \"OrcaSlicer AI redesign concepts\" (claude.ai/design/p/d981c5e2-…, files like `Orca Chat Panel.dc.html`). It is history for how a decision was reached, never the current design. For the chat panel, including G-code entries and print bands, the current boards are the five `main-print-timeline-panel-full*` boards on the canvas's Main Page. **The canvas moved (2026-10-27):** VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v is itself frozen (\"JusPrin v2 (frozen 2026-10-27)\" title, a `frozen-pointer-*` note on every page). The current canvas is https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, with numbered board names (`main-05-print-timeline-panel-full-no-revert`, `main-07-…full`, `agent-ui-01-timeline-cards-manufacturing-history-state-matrix`) and shared parts as `<dc-import>` components that render.py can't draw. Check the canvas title before editing. On it (version 1793132250-e29e) `plates-26e3-project-print-history` and the state matrix were redrawn to the G-code design (matrix now 3 variants, 772 px tall). I also edited 26e3 on the frozen canvas by mistake (version 1793132033-a81d); at Kenneth's request it was restored byte-for-byte to the original BUILD 1 board in version 1793132895-0706.\n\n**How to apply:** when a memory note, commit message, doc or old plan cites a Figma frame, node id or value, treat it as history and check the artifact board instead. Edit the artifacts directly (recipe in [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]]); never re-sync them from Figma, which would overwrite newer design.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"21a80ee5-c679-4fc4-8f96-ebaa5d9809f1","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:20:51.212Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: first-run-flow-boards\ndescription: \"First-launch boards on the canvas onboarding page: variants A/B withdrawn 2026-11-02; Kenneth's one split welcome screen drawn as first-run-welcome-01..03 (version 87; no chrome + corner lockup in 88; the flow 04-11 in 89); builder build_first_run_page.py.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438\n  modified: 2026-11-03T03:48:37.053Z\n---\n\n2026-11-02: the no-wizard variants A and B (`first-run-a-*`, `first-run-b-*`) were withdrawn at Kenneth's request and removed in canvas version 87. Nothing else on the page had moved for them. In their place, `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1`, `-02-clip-final-frame` and `-03-clip-storyboard` draw the welcome screen from [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]]. Version 88 made it a full-window screen with no shell header or footer and the JusPrin lockup in the top-left corner (43 px tall, space-24/space-16), Kenneth's \"Lockup\" choice. They are built by `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`.\n\nGaps at the time: the type scale has no display size for the clip's big settings (page-title is used); there are no boards after \"Just slice for now\"; and nothing on the canvas now shows the \"assumed\" printer chip.\n\nFacts from the variant work that still apply: `printer_from_file` (`!is_named_printer`) would label an assumed default \"from the file\"; an empty data folder has no printers; the project chat can't add a printer; Home has no agent pane.\n\n**Why:** later sessions may find references to A/B and assume they are current.\n\n**How to apply:** treat A/B as history. Build the first launch from the welcome boards and the decision memory. Related: [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]], [[credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages]].\n\n**2026-11-03, version 93 (1793744174-5990), canvas ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ:** the boards now draw the built sign-in door. 01/02: Continue with Google, \"or\", email field + Continue with email, Terms line; 04: the browser-wait card (\"Nothing happened? Open the browser again\", \"Use an email code instead\"); 05: \"Signed in as alex@example.com · 500 credits\"; 10: Home's \"Set up the agent\" with the same door. New row y 7100: 12 email choice (Email me a 6-digit code, or password + Sign in), 13 wrong password, 14 typing the code, 15 wrong code, 16 code no longer works. Rows 07-08 and 09-10 and the superseded wizard moved down 940. The free doors dim only once signed in. Work copy `figma-mirror/work-first-run-door/`. Home's narrow column truncates the email field placeholder (\"you@exar\") — the app has the same CSS, so it likely looks the same there.\n---\nname: render-canvas-boards-with-render-dc\ndescription: \"figma-mirror/tools/composer/render_dc.py renders canvas boards to PNG through the canvas's own runtime, so dc-imports draw; render.py leaves them blank. Needs a work dir holding the live files and runtime/.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 3eabf4a3-87b6-4471-a4e5-b6fb9c14763a\n  modified: 2026-11-02T03:18:24.462Z\n---\n\n`python3 figma-mirror/tools/composer/render_dc.py <work dir> <out dir> [--dark] <board.dc.html>...` serves `<work>/project`, maps `support.js` to `<work>/runtime/dc-runtime.js` (the artifact's `artifact-type/dc-runtime.js`) and `/_blob/<id>` through `<work>/runtime/blobs.json`, and shoots headless Chrome at 2x with its own `--user-data-dir`. 21 boards take about 22 s. `--dark` flips the board's theme prop. A working `work-credits/` exists from the 2026-11-01 credits page.\n\nAlso learned drawing that page: anything absolutely placed over the Prepare screen needs a z-index above the composer band's, or the band paints over it. `figma-mirror/published/canvas` is stale (old board names), so pull live files with Artifact read `paths` + `out_dir` rather than copying from it. Related: [[canvas-boards-from-bundle-rules]], [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]].\n---\nname: design-source-is-claude-artifacts\ndescription: \"2026-10-20: Figma is retired for JusPrin design; the Claude Design System and JusPrin v2 canvas artifacts are the source of truth. Don't propose Figma changes or cite Figma.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 1ad40aa6-b204-449c-8be8-7600964a4f52\n  modified: 2026-10-27T20:28:20.888Z\n---\n\nKenneth, 2026-10-20: \"We're not changing Figma anymore. We have migrated to\nCloud artifact.\" The two Claude artifacts are now the design source of truth:\nthe Design System (https://claude.ai/artifact/3zgiix8rAw3rXextQnR5UL) and the\n\"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v). They\nstarted as copies of Figma ([[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]]), but\nthey are no longer re-synced from it.\n\n**Why:** design changes now happen in the artifacts, so a Figma-based argument\nor a \"change Figma\" proposal points at a dead file.\n\n**How to apply:** check designs by reading the artifact files (Artifact read\nwith `path`, e.g. `project/<page>-<frame>.dc.html` on the canvas); never\nsuggest editing Figma or waiting for Figma seat allowance; when citing a\ndesign, name the artifact board, not a Figma node. Describe what the board\nactually draws, not what a component's internal properties imply: a menu row\nwith no fill or border draws no shape at all, so it is not \"a square row\".\nOlder memories that say \"Figma is the source of truth\"\n([[design-token-sync-decisions]], [[figma-jusprin-v2-file]]) are superseded on\nthat point.\n\n**Restated by Kenneth later on 2026-10-20:** \"from now on, we should assume claude design artifact is the up to date design. figma is out of date.\" Docs changed the same day (uncommitted on jusprin-newui): agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md no longer points at Figma, and the repo skill .claude/skills/figma-agent-design is marked retired.\n\n**Also frozen (Kenneth, 2026-10-27):** the old Claude Design project \"OrcaSlicer AI redesign concepts\" (claude.ai/design/p/d981c5e2-…, files like `Orca Chat Panel.dc.html`). It is history for how a decision was reached, never the current design. For the chat panel, including G-code entries and print bands, the current boards are the five `main-print-timeline-panel-full*` boards on the canvas's Main Page. **The canvas moved (2026-10-27):** VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v is itself frozen (\"JusPrin v2 (frozen 2026-10-27)\" title, a `frozen-pointer-*` note on every page). The current canvas is https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, with numbered board names (`main-05-print-timeline-panel-full-no-revert`, `main-07-…full`, `agent-ui-01-timeline-cards-manufacturing-history-state-matrix`) and shared parts as `<dc-import>` components that render.py can't draw. Check the canvas title before editing. On it (version 1793132250-e29e) `plates-26e3-project-print-history` and the state matrix were redrawn to the G-code design (matrix now 3 variants, 772 px tall). I also edited 26e3 on the frozen canvas by mistake (version 1793132033-a81d); at Kenneth's request it was restored byte-for-byte to the original BUILD 1 board in version 1793132895-0706.\n\n**How to apply:** when a memory note, commit message, doc or old plan cites a Figma frame, node id or value, treat it as history and check the artifact board instead. Edit the artifacts directly (recipe in [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]]); never re-sync them from Figma, which would overwrite newer design.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"be5d640d-3f38-4392-acce-16ff509fcb6b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-printer-step","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
