{"parentUuid":"42ad2a5e-e720-4cdc-9d7c-3c8a8f6c2f4f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkon83ndAqPm393auHx2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015NBp7ThCAFXnEBEjwYY5aH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/cmake-file-edit-forces-full-rebuild.md | sed -n 1,30p"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":888,"cache_read_input_tokens":270301,"output_tokens":218,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":101},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":888,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":218,"cache_read_input_tokens":270301,"cache_creation_input_tokens":888,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":888},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015NBp7ThCAFXnEBEjwYY5aH":{"command":"cat /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/cmake-file-edit-forces-full-rebuild.md | sed -n 1,30p"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgkon7nfFhpWaydFfovtr","requestRef":"f9800e11-9d7b-4a4d-867e-2859f9c3f496","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"61e40121-bc42-464a-aa0c-d8acaf080680","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:28:55.317Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"61e40121-bc42-464a-aa0c-d8acaf080680","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4fcc31c2-3e80-420b-a5c6-f7cbf63689ec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015NBp7ThCAFXnEBEjwYY5aH","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: cmake-file-edit-forces-full-rebuild\ndescription: \"Editing sources.cmake, or adding a file to a globbed directory such as a new AgentUI skill, after a commit re-runs CMake, which bakes the new HEAD into -DGIT_COMMIT_HASH on every compile line, so ninja rebuilds all ~970 steps.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 62f57a5d-138a-485a-ac71-94d683a8c5db\n  modified: 2026-11-01T13:16:25.404Z\n---\n\n2026-10-24 (import-behavior work, PR TheSpaghettiDetective/JusPrin#38): adding EmptyPlateHint.cpp to `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/sources.cmake` after committing made the next build re-run CMake. The configure step reads the git hash into `-DGIT_COMMIT_HASH=\\\"<sha>\\\"`, which is on every TU's command line, so the whole tree (libslic3r included) recompiled at -j4: roughly an hour.\n\nNot the only cause of that symptom: if the build log starts with \"premature end of file; recovering\", see [[ninja-deps-bad-record-repeat-rebuild]].\n\n2026-11-02 (connection-skill worktree): adding two new `AgentUI/src/skills/*/SKILL.md` files did the same. The jusprin_web target globs that tree, so the build printed \"GLOB mismatch!\", re-ran CMake and started 945 steps for jusprin_web + agent_bridge_tests + shell_integration_harness.\n\n**Why:** a command-line change invalidates every object in ninja's log, not just the touched target.\n**How to apply:** add new source files to `sources.cmake`, and new skill or other globbed files, before the first build of a worktree, and avoid committing between a cmake-file edit and the build that needs it. Related: [[jusprin-worktree-build]], [[pkill-cmake-build-leaves-ninja]].\n\nAlso learned that day: OrcaSlicer reinstalls its own `PlaterDropTarget` after every slice completes (`Plater::priv::on_process_completed`, `is_finished` is true for every non-slice-all run), so any fork-owned Plater drop target must be put back afterwards (the shell does it on idle).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a9f7b401-53b2-4326-951d-2dd2335bf501","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:28:55.367Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: cmake-file-edit-forces-full-rebuild\ndescription: \"Editing sources.cmake, or adding a file to a globbed directory such as a new AgentUI skill, after a commit re-runs CMake, which bakes the new HEAD into -DGIT_COMMIT_HASH on every compile line, so ninja rebuilds all ~970 steps.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 62f57a5d-138a-485a-ac71-94d683a8c5db\n  modified: 2026-11-01T13:16:25.404Z\n---\n\n2026-10-24 (import-behavior work, PR TheSpaghettiDetective/JusPrin#38): adding EmptyPlateHint.cpp to `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/sources.cmake` after committing made the next build re-run CMake. The configure step reads the git hash into `-DGIT_COMMIT_HASH=\\\"<sha>\\\"`, which is on every TU's command line, so the whole tree (libslic3r included) recompiled at -j4: roughly an hour.\n\nNot the only cause of that symptom: if the build log starts with \"premature end of file; recovering\", see [[ninja-deps-bad-record-repeat-rebuild]].\n\n2026-11-02 (connection-skill worktree): adding two new `AgentUI/src/skills/*/SKILL.md` files did the same. The jusprin_web target globs that tree, so the build printed \"GLOB mismatch!\", re-ran CMake and started 945 steps for jusprin_web + agent_bridge_tests + shell_integration_harness.\n\n**Why:** a command-line change invalidates every object in ninja's log, not just the touched target.\n**How to apply:** add new source files to `sources.cmake`, and new skill or other globbed files, before the first build of a worktree, and avoid committing between a cmake-file edit and the build that needs it. Related: [[jusprin-worktree-build]], [[pkill-cmake-build-leaves-ninja]].\n\nAlso learned that day: OrcaSlicer reinstalls its own `PlaterDropTarget` after every slice completes (`Plater::priv::on_process_completed`, `is_finished` is true for every non-slice-all run), so any fork-owned Plater drop target must be put back afterwards (the shell does it on idle).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"61e40121-bc42-464a-aa0c-d8acaf080680","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
