{"parentUuid":"e7d48dd9-41fc-4043-b7df-fd0f2a857eeb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkpD2MvNyHR6XcpbQMV4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011uerB78AXDrUuznMJQ5NPr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35; awk '/^## Writing UI code/{f=1} f' agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md | head -60; grep -n \"secondary\" src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/styles.css | grep \"^[0-9]*:button\\|^[0-9]*:\\.button\\|button-secondary\" | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_read_input_tokens":318781,"output_tokens":315,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":111},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1125,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":318781,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1125},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011uerB78AXDrUuznMJQ5NPr":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35; awk '/^## Writing UI code/{f=1} f' agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md | head -60; grep -n \"secondary\" src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/styles.css | grep \"^[0-9]*:button\\|^[0-9]*:\\.button\\|button-secondary\" | head"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgkpD28H8S2D6hLcbeS6S","requestRef":"4e4ff854-beac-43b6-b43f-c8c95e034c65","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5a924bc1-96db-41a7-ab40-4071d2ef7826","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:34:35.212Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"5a924bc1-96db-41a7-ab40-4071d2ef7826","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4fcc31c2-3e80-420b-a5c6-f7cbf63689ec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011uerB78AXDrUuznMJQ5NPr","type":"tool_result","content":"## Writing UI code\n\nRules for anyone, human or agent, adding or changing a JusPrin surface. They\nexist because every value that is typed by hand drifts from the design system and\nfrom the other side of the app within weeks; today's guards catch most of it, but\nonly if the code goes through the token file in the first place.\n\n1. **Never type a color, radius, font, or control size.** Every one comes\n   from `resources/jusprin/ui/design-tokens.json`. Native code reads it\n   through `ShellTheme`: `palette(dark)` for color, `metrics()` for radii,\n   spacing, and per-component sizes, `font(role)` for type. A stock\n   `wxStaticText`, `wxTextCtrl`, or OrcaSlicer `Button` is\n   dressed through `Shell/ShellRecipes.hpp`, never by calling its setters\n   with literals. The Agent page uses only `var(--…)`: `--<group>-<name>` for\n   color, `--radius-<name>`, `--font-<role>`, `--font-code`, and\n   `--button-<recipe>-padding`.\n2. **If the value you need has no token, add the token first.** Put it in\n   the JSON, extend the guard in `tests/brand/test_brand_tokens.cpp` so a\n   later edit cannot silently move it, then read it from code. Do not write\n   the number \"for now\": the guards cannot see a literal that is already\n   there, and the next reader cannot tell a decision from an accident. A\n   value that exists in the design artifacts but not in the roles or scales is a design\n   decision to raise, not a reason to type it.\n3. **Layout spacing may stay literal, on the scale.** Padding between\n   regions, gaps, and margins use 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, or 48 DIP.\n   Control padding is not layout spacing; it comes from a button recipe.\n4. **Pick the nearest role, never a bespoke size.** The roles are the whole\n   type system. Bold at a body or label size is a role of its own; if a\n   surface seems to need a size that no role has, see rule 2.\n5. **The design system wins when it and the code disagree.** The two Claude\n   artifacts are the source of truth (Kenneth, 2026-10-20; Figma is\n   retired): the Design System\n   (https://claude.ai/artifact/3zgiix8rAw3rXextQnR5UL) and the \"JusPrin v2\"\n   canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ). The canvas\n   frozen on 2026-10-27 (https://claude.ai/artifact/VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v)\n   is history, not a source. Change the token file to match, or, when the\n   code's value is the one to keep, change the artifact first. Do not trust\n   old commit messages about either.\n6. **Run the guards before calling UI work done:** `brand_tokens_tests`,\n   `shell_theme_tests`, and `npm test` in `AgentUI`. Then look at the surface\n   in the running app; the guards prove the code went through the tokens,\n   not that the result looks right.\n7. **Upstream files are off limits for style.** OrcaSlicer's own screens are\n   retinted through the hooks `BrandPalette.cpp` installs and nothing else;\n   see [Fork stewardship](fork-stewardship.md). Their radii and fonts stay\n   OrcaSlicer's until the surface is replaced.\n\n## Runtime application in the native app\n\nThe token file is applied to the running application in three layers. All\nthree read `resources/jusprin/ui/design-tokens.json`; none of them carries a\ncolor literal of its own, and the whole layer touches OrcaSlicer code in only\nthree small, additive seams plus one attachment point.\n\n1. **Fork-owned surfaces** (`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/*`, the React Agent\n   page) resolve every style through the token file, not only color.\n   - Native: `ShellTheme` exposes `palette(dark)` for color, `metrics()` for\n     the radius and spacing scales and the per-component sizes, `font(role)`\n     for the type roles above. It is loaded once, by `Brand/BrandPalette.cpp`, and passed\n     by reference into every shell widget. Widgets that paint themselves read\n602:.chat-dialog-buttons button { gap: var(--button-secondary-icon-gap); min-height: var(--button-secondary-height); padding: var(--button-secondary-padding); border-color: var(--border-subtle); background: var(--surface-raised); font: var(--font-body-small); }\n1040:.proposal-actions > button:not(.primary) { min-height: var(--button-secondary-height); padding: var(--button-secondary-padding); border-color: var(--border-subtle); font: var(--font-body-small); }\n1231:.change-revert-buttons button { min-height: var(--button-secondary-height); padding: var(--button-secondary-padding); font: var(--font-body-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); }\n1294:  gap: var(--button-secondary-icon-gap);\n1295:  min-height: var(--button-secondary-height);\n1296:  padding: var(--button-secondary-padding);\n1489:  padding: var(--button-secondary-padding);\n2173:  height: var(--button-secondary-small-height);\n2174:  padding: var(--button-secondary-small-padding);\n2255:  min-height: var(--button-secondary-height);","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d2c2f5d4-bcdc-474d-8154-6f99cbeee3c8","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:34:35.400Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Writing UI code\n\nRules for anyone, human or agent, adding or changing a JusPrin surface. They\nexist because every value that is typed by hand drifts from the design system and\nfrom the other side of the app within weeks; today's guards catch most of it, but\nonly if the code goes through the token file in the first place.\n\n1. **Never type a color, radius, font, or control size.** Every one comes\n   from `resources/jusprin/ui/design-tokens.json`. Native code reads it\n   through `ShellTheme`: `palette(dark)` for color, `metrics()` for radii,\n   spacing, and per-component sizes, `font(role)` for type. A stock\n   `wxStaticText`, `wxTextCtrl`, or OrcaSlicer `Button` is\n   dressed through `Shell/ShellRecipes.hpp`, never by calling its setters\n   with literals. The Agent page uses only `var(--…)`: `--<group>-<name>` for\n   color, `--radius-<name>`, `--font-<role>`, `--font-code`, and\n   `--button-<recipe>-padding`.\n2. **If the value you need has no token, add the token first.** Put it in\n   the JSON, extend the guard in `tests/brand/test_brand_tokens.cpp` so a\n   later edit cannot silently move it, then read it from code. Do not write\n   the number \"for now\": the guards cannot see a literal that is already\n   there, and the next reader cannot tell a decision from an accident. A\n   value that exists in the design artifacts but not in the roles or scales is a design\n   decision to raise, not a reason to type it.\n3. **Layout spacing may stay literal, on the scale.** Padding between\n   regions, gaps, and margins use 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, or 48 DIP.\n   Control padding is not layout spacing; it comes from a button recipe.\n4. **Pick the nearest role, never a bespoke size.** The roles are the whole\n   type system. Bold at a body or label size is a role of its own; if a\n   surface seems to need a size that no role has, see rule 2.\n5. **The design system wins when it and the code disagree.** The two Claude\n   artifacts are the source of truth (Kenneth, 2026-10-20; Figma is\n   retired): the Design System\n   (https://claude.ai/artifact/3zgiix8rAw3rXextQnR5UL) and the \"JusPrin v2\"\n   canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ). The canvas\n   frozen on 2026-10-27 (https://claude.ai/artifact/VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v)\n   is history, not a source. Change the token file to match, or, when the\n   code's value is the one to keep, change the artifact first. Do not trust\n   old commit messages about either.\n6. **Run the guards before calling UI work done:** `brand_tokens_tests`,\n   `shell_theme_tests`, and `npm test` in `AgentUI`. Then look at the surface\n   in the running app; the guards prove the code went through the tokens,\n   not that the result looks right.\n7. **Upstream files are off limits for style.** OrcaSlicer's own screens are\n   retinted through the hooks `BrandPalette.cpp` installs and nothing else;\n   see [Fork stewardship](fork-stewardship.md). Their radii and fonts stay\n   OrcaSlicer's until the surface is replaced.\n\n## Runtime application in the native app\n\nThe token file is applied to the running application in three layers. All\nthree read `resources/jusprin/ui/design-tokens.json`; none of them carries a\ncolor literal of its own, and the whole layer touches OrcaSlicer code in only\nthree small, additive seams plus one attachment point.\n\n1. **Fork-owned surfaces** (`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/*`, the React Agent\n   page) resolve every style through the token file, not only color.\n   - Native: `ShellTheme` exposes `palette(dark)` for color, `metrics()` for\n     the radius and spacing scales and the per-component sizes, `font(role)`\n     for the type roles above. It is loaded once, by `Brand/BrandPalette.cpp`, and passed\n     by reference into every shell widget. Widgets that paint themselves read\n602:.chat-dialog-buttons button { gap: var(--button-secondary-icon-gap); min-height: var(--button-secondary-height); padding: var(--button-secondary-padding); border-color: var(--border-subtle); background: var(--surface-raised); font: var(--font-body-small); }\n1040:.proposal-actions > button:not(.primary) { min-height: var(--button-secondary-height); padding: var(--button-secondary-padding); border-color: var(--border-subtle); font: var(--font-body-small); }\n1231:.change-revert-buttons button { min-height: var(--button-secondary-height); padding: var(--button-secondary-padding); font: var(--font-body-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); }\n1294:  gap: var(--button-secondary-icon-gap);\n1295:  min-height: var(--button-secondary-height);\n1296:  padding: var(--button-secondary-padding);\n1489:  padding: var(--button-secondary-padding);\n2173:  height: var(--button-secondary-small-height);\n2174:  padding: var(--button-secondary-small-padding);\n2255:  min-height: var(--button-secondary-height);","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5a924bc1-96db-41a7-ab40-4071d2ef7826","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
