{"parentUuid":"52dd474c-41d6-4c64-b4a0-7b3905cf1bed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkpx8RkSBZ1C9KRobkyS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HXz1FBWW9D7cdeMbGW1ze1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"M=/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory; cat $M/ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe.md $M/scratch-app-driving-traps.md | head -80; cat /private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin--claude-worktrees-first-run-flow-f7be35/c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983/scratchpad/pstep/launch.sh","description":"Read app-driving notes and launch script"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1163,"cache_read_input_tokens":118940,"output_tokens":340,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":79},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1163,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":340,"cache_read_input_tokens":118940,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1163,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1163},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HXz1FBWW9D7cdeMbGW1ze1":{"command":"M=/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory; cat $M/ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe.md $M/scratch-app-driving-traps.md | head -80; cat /private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin--claude-worktrees-first-run-flow-f7be35/c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983/scratchpad/pstep/launch.sh","description":"Read app-driving notes and launch script"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgkpx8CMUM4LJiuYb6Hp5","requestRef":"360923f4-fb33-4b80-9cc8-3d185f5c0f30","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"404859d1-69d1-4933-9c4a-cf2a9a54df23","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:44:18.749Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"404859d1-69d1-4933-9c4a-cf2a9a54df23","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4fcc31c2-3e80-420b-a5c6-f7cbf63689ec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HXz1FBWW9D7cdeMbGW1ze1","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe\ndescription: \"How to drive the real built JusPrin app for a screenshot-per-step UX walkthrough (2026-10-28): scratch copies, the empty local_machines loop with the fake printer, why background app_* tools fail on Orca dialogs, and where screenshots land.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 33551592-d22c-4161-9a14-9a22ef798541\n  modified: 2026-10-28T13:12:42.393Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-10-28 I walked six scenarios (open-and-print, fix-a-problem) through the real app with Opus 5.5 and published the critique at https://claude.ai/artifact/XyVvteGiKhiJ6apUx8rcmR (34 frames, scratch copy at scratchpad/ux/ of that session). Kenneth's steer: start from files people actually download (MakerWorld 3MFs carry a full Bambu profile: printer, print preset, filaments, colours, bed type, designer, licence), not from generated STLs. `~/Downloads` has Tape_4_3MF.3mf (A1 mini profile), find_my_hollow.3mf (P1S, 3 colours, 233 mm wide, too big for an A1 mini), arrow_headband.3mf (P1S), general_purpose_hook.STL (bare).\n\n**Recipe that worked**\n- `ditto` the built .app out of `build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/` into the scratchpad before launching (another session's ninja can relink it underneath you); the bundle id is already unique (`io.jusprin.JusPrin`), no re-sign needed.\n- `ditto` `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2` to a scratch `--datadir`; set `jusprin.fake_printer=true`, `presets.machine` to the saved \"Bambu Lab A1 mini 2\", write `jusprin/fake_printer.json`, delete `jusprin/mcp.json.lock`.\n- **Clear `local_machines`.** Kenneth's conf carries a `local_machines` entry keyed by the empty string (old Moonraker experiment). With the fake Bambu agent on, `init_networking_callbacks`' connect callback calls `DeviceManager::set_selected_machine(\"\")` in a loop (\"same lan machine, dev_id =, disconnect and reconnect\"), the main window disappears and the log grew 700 MB in two minutes. Clearing the map fixed it. The loop has no guard; see [[fake-bambu-printer-sim]] and [[harness-fake-printer-cleanup]].\n- Background `app_*` tools cannot press OrcaSlicer's custom `Button`s (no AX action) and the hit test at the dialog's screen position reports \"belongs to a different process\". `request_full_control` + `computer_batch` works for everything, including the Agent web view and the macOS file chooser (`cmd+shift+g`, type the path, Return, Return). Re-front the app with `open_application` when another session's harness steals focus.\n- Every `app_screenshot`/`computer_batch` screenshot is written as a JPEG under `~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session>/tool-results/mcp-computer-use-blob-*.jpg`; copy those for a report instead of fighting `screencapture`.\n- The dev build (-O0) slices a 38 mm part in over a minute; wait 45–60 s before judging a slice.\n\n**Why:** the first launch attempt looked like an app bug (blank window, title \"Couldn't save\") and cost ten minutes; the dialog-click refusals cost another ten.\n**How to apply:** reuse this for any \"walk through the app as a user\" request; keep scenarios on downloaded files; write the critique per step as what the person knows / sees / finds confusing. Related: [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[drive-app-with-posted-key-events]].\n---\nname: scratch-app-driving-traps\ndescription: \"Five traps met driving a scratch copy of the built app without screen control (2026-11-04): in-place binary copy gets SIGKILL, Home drops bridge messages while hidden, header popups need a posted NSEvent, lldb std::string args, wx Wrap reuse.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: dea8379c-b02c-43a2-a254-4c2259672439\n  modified: 2026-11-04T18:59:38.548Z\n---\n\nMet while verifying print-host printer window fixes on the scratch `.app` (see [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[open-file-in-app-without-screen-control]]).\n\n- **Copy a new build into a `.app` with `rm` then `cp`.** `cp` over the existing signed binary keeps the inode; the kernel kills the launch at once (exit 137, nothing logged).\n- **A launch from a plain Bash call dies when the call ends.** Start the app with `run_in_background: true` and `exec`.\n- **Home ignores bridge messages while the main window shows a project.** A queued `launch_monitor` through `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` is sent by the page and silently dropped; switch to Home first (`m_tabpanel->SetSelection(0)` via lldb).\n- **Background `app_click` does not reach the header's popup menus** (they are not listed as windows). Post the click into the app's queue with lldb: `expr -l objc -- @import AppKit`, then `NSEvent mouseEventWithType:NSEventTypeLeftMouseDown/Up location:NSMakePoint(x, y-from-popup-bottom) ... windowNumber:[popup windowNumber]` and `[NSApp postEvent:atStart:NO]`. Render the popup with `cacheDisplayInRect:` on its contentView ([[capture-mac-popups-for-platform-diff]]).\n- **lldb cannot build `std::string` args.** This libc++ uses the alternate short-string layout: a 24-byte char array with the text at offset 0 and its length in byte 23 (≤ 22 chars), passed as `*(std::string*)buf`.\n- **wx `wxStaticText::Wrap()` (Orca's wx) skips a width it already wrapped at and keeps the first text it wrapped**, so SetLabel + Wrap on a reused label comes back unwrapped. Use a fresh label.\n#!/bin/zsh\n# launch.sh <case-dir> : runs the scratch app on <case-dir>/JusPrin, Home from the dev page, account at the fake gateway\nS=${0:a:h}\nexec env JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8767/page.html JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8767/agent.html JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8767/v1/responses \\\n  $S/JusPrinTest.app/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer --datadir $1/JusPrin > $1.out 2>&1","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"99e3e057-00ee-4787-b4c2-10836f164e88","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:44:19.060Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe\ndescription: \"How to drive the real built JusPrin app for a screenshot-per-step UX walkthrough (2026-10-28): scratch copies, the empty local_machines loop with the fake printer, why background app_* tools fail on Orca dialogs, and where screenshots land.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 33551592-d22c-4161-9a14-9a22ef798541\n  modified: 2026-10-28T13:12:42.393Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-10-28 I walked six scenarios (open-and-print, fix-a-problem) through the real app with Opus 5.5 and published the critique at https://claude.ai/artifact/XyVvteGiKhiJ6apUx8rcmR (34 frames, scratch copy at scratchpad/ux/ of that session). Kenneth's steer: start from files people actually download (MakerWorld 3MFs carry a full Bambu profile: printer, print preset, filaments, colours, bed type, designer, licence), not from generated STLs. `~/Downloads` has Tape_4_3MF.3mf (A1 mini profile), find_my_hollow.3mf (P1S, 3 colours, 233 mm wide, too big for an A1 mini), arrow_headband.3mf (P1S), general_purpose_hook.STL (bare).\n\n**Recipe that worked**\n- `ditto` the built .app out of `build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/` into the scratchpad before launching (another session's ninja can relink it underneath you); the bundle id is already unique (`io.jusprin.JusPrin`), no re-sign needed.\n- `ditto` `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2` to a scratch `--datadir`; set `jusprin.fake_printer=true`, `presets.machine` to the saved \"Bambu Lab A1 mini 2\", write `jusprin/fake_printer.json`, delete `jusprin/mcp.json.lock`.\n- **Clear `local_machines`.** Kenneth's conf carries a `local_machines` entry keyed by the empty string (old Moonraker experiment). With the fake Bambu agent on, `init_networking_callbacks`' connect callback calls `DeviceManager::set_selected_machine(\"\")` in a loop (\"same lan machine, dev_id =, disconnect and reconnect\"), the main window disappears and the log grew 700 MB in two minutes. Clearing the map fixed it. The loop has no guard; see [[fake-bambu-printer-sim]] and [[harness-fake-printer-cleanup]].\n- Background `app_*` tools cannot press OrcaSlicer's custom `Button`s (no AX action) and the hit test at the dialog's screen position reports \"belongs to a different process\". `request_full_control` + `computer_batch` works for everything, including the Agent web view and the macOS file chooser (`cmd+shift+g`, type the path, Return, Return). Re-front the app with `open_application` when another session's harness steals focus.\n- Every `app_screenshot`/`computer_batch` screenshot is written as a JPEG under `~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session>/tool-results/mcp-computer-use-blob-*.jpg`; copy those for a report instead of fighting `screencapture`.\n- The dev build (-O0) slices a 38 mm part in over a minute; wait 45–60 s before judging a slice.\n\n**Why:** the first launch attempt looked like an app bug (blank window, title \"Couldn't save\") and cost ten minutes; the dialog-click refusals cost another ten.\n**How to apply:** reuse this for any \"walk through the app as a user\" request; keep scenarios on downloaded files; write the critique per step as what the person knows / sees / finds confusing. Related: [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[drive-app-with-posted-key-events]].\n---\nname: scratch-app-driving-traps\ndescription: \"Five traps met driving a scratch copy of the built app without screen control (2026-11-04): in-place binary copy gets SIGKILL, Home drops bridge messages while hidden, header popups need a posted NSEvent, lldb std::string args, wx Wrap reuse.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: dea8379c-b02c-43a2-a254-4c2259672439\n  modified: 2026-11-04T18:59:38.548Z\n---\n\nMet while verifying print-host printer window fixes on the scratch `.app` (see [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[open-file-in-app-without-screen-control]]).\n\n- **Copy a new build into a `.app` with `rm` then `cp`.** `cp` over the existing signed binary keeps the inode; the kernel kills the launch at once (exit 137, nothing logged).\n- **A launch from a plain Bash call dies when the call ends.** Start the app with `run_in_background: true` and `exec`.\n- **Home ignores bridge messages while the main window shows a project.** A queued `launch_monitor` through `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` is sent by the page and silently dropped; switch to Home first (`m_tabpanel->SetSelection(0)` via lldb).\n- **Background `app_click` does not reach the header's popup menus** (they are not listed as windows). Post the click into the app's queue with lldb: `expr -l objc -- @import AppKit`, then `NSEvent mouseEventWithType:NSEventTypeLeftMouseDown/Up location:NSMakePoint(x, y-from-popup-bottom) ... windowNumber:[popup windowNumber]` and `[NSApp postEvent:atStart:NO]`. Render the popup with `cacheDisplayInRect:` on its contentView ([[capture-mac-popups-for-platform-diff]]).\n- **lldb cannot build `std::string` args.** This libc++ uses the alternate short-string layout: a 24-byte char array with the text at offset 0 and its length in byte 23 (≤ 22 chars), passed as `*(std::string*)buf`.\n- **wx `wxStaticText::Wrap()` (Orca's wx) skips a width it already wrapped at and keeps the first text it wrapped**, so SetLabel + Wrap on a reused label comes back unwrapped. Use a fresh label.\n#!/bin/zsh\n# launch.sh <case-dir> : runs the scratch app on <case-dir>/JusPrin, Home from the dev page, account at the fake gateway\nS=${0:a:h}\nexec env JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8767/page.html JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8767/agent.html JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8767/v1/responses \\\n  $S/JusPrinTest.app/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer --datadir $1/JusPrin > $1.out 2>&1","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"404859d1-69d1-4933-9c4a-cf2a9a54df23","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
