{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","id":"0fc83662-647c-4619-9262-a3fe46b22c01","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:22:51.456Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"6be4cbcf13bd24f91c1084271e54c66443d4511e9a00e5bc8042b89ce33d2e34","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"a9b20954-7509-43f9-9689-17d48932434c","keep":269,"tail":["82f7600357112ee910ecba390429b282b42a35433e5485413c36d362ebb4368d","14181b17cc7309318881bc73375b6884cc5e0825d072b793f20acead27131ec5","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",271,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"90e2ab166608e89110e6af91e77e69975b8d13f7c928c264292ae3273b26ea64"}
{"parentUuid":"d4edd244-cf1f-42c4-a0f9-a393a6862434","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkstwUx7h393ssK84Cuh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Commit ee3a17e64b on branch `claude/orca-import-menu` adds File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer…, and all three proofs you asked for pass in the built app. It's not pushed or merged.\n\n**What the item does:** it's the last entry in File › Import, after \"Import Configs…\". It opens a window over the current screen that lists OrcaSlicer's printers and marks the ones JusPrin already has as \"Already in JusPrin\". The first launch and the menu now share the same import code. The only change to OrcaSlicer's own code is one added `append_menu_item` line in MainFrame.cpp. The commit message says where that line must stay at each rebase.\n\n**Tests:** all pass. That's 166 C++ test cases, the brand-token and theme suites, and 674 page tests. On a copy of Kenneth's OrcaSlicer folder in a separate copy of the app:\n- **First import:** brought 8 printers and 3 filaments.\n- **Second import:** showed \"Every printer in this OrcaSlicer folder is already in JusPrin\". JusPrin's user preset folder has no \"(Orca copy)\" files.\n- **Third import, after I added one new printer to the OrcaSlicer copy:** imported only that printer, and the project kept Bambu Lab P1S.\n- **No folder:** a data folder with no OrcaSlicer folder beside it showed \"JusPrin didn't find OrcaSlicer's folder…\" with the path it looked in.\n\nScreenshots of each screen are in `orca-import-menu/` in the shared notes folder.\n\n**Two problems the live test caught, both fixed:**\n- **Duplicate filament on the second import.** OrcaSlicer's \"Elegoo Generic ABS - Copy\" is based on \"Elegoo Generic ABS\". JusPrin doesn't have that base, so OrcaSlicer's preset loader swaps in \"Generic ABS @System\", and the imported copy is saved with that base. The \"same name and same base\" check never matched, so every run offered the filament again and would have saved it as \"(Orca copy)\". The check now compares the base under the name JusPrin actually loaded. A unit test covers this case.\n- **The printer list hid \"Choose another folder…\".** With 8 printers the folder row sat below the window edge. The list now scrolls inside the window.\n\n**Proposal — my call, not agreed by Kenneth:** the import keeps the project's printer, except when the selected printer is the \"Generic printer\" the first launch installs for someone who named none. Keeping that one selected was wrong. Home hides that card once a real printer exists and then says \"JusPrin slices it for your Anycubic Kobra 3\", while a newly opened model would still slice for the hidden generic printer. So in that one case the import selects OrcaSlicer's selected printer, as the first launch does. The result then says \"JusPrin now uses Bambu Lab P1S in place of the generic printer.\"\n\n**Not built as drawn:**\n- Printer rows show no filament count.\n- There is an extra screen for a chosen folder that holds no printers.\n- The title is in the window's title bar, not drawn in the page.\n- When only filaments or settings are new, the button reads \"Import\".\n\n**Still needs Kenneth:**\n- He hasn't agreed to the two rules from the design session. One is that \"already has\" means the same name and the same base; the other is that the menu import keeps the project's printer.\n- Whether to merge or push this branch, `claude/first-run-printer-step` and `claude/encrypted-token-file` is still open.\n- Unverified: if an import switches printers back and forth, the project's wipe-tower position may reset to its default. I didn't check this."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":408,"cache_read_input_tokens":282591,"output_tokens":1206,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":408,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1206,"cache_read_input_tokens":282591,"cache_creation_input_tokens":408,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":408},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgkstw8MxGLTjqWYyHvz3","requestRef":"0fc83662-647c-4619-9262-a3fe46b22c01","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"98c71b00-cb45-411c-aa23-886130a206c2","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:23:02.317Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
