{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:23:31.131Z","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","content":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): allauth-upgrade = local_2c0bf928-2175-4569-9108-2cb6cba1fb77 (idle); use-a-jusprin-syndicate = local_69a34677-cdae-4851-90bb-557cd0ba6d32 (idle); design-the-no-wizard-fir = local_e71c8b0a-6720-4250-85de-80d4899e6200 (idle). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_e71c8b0a-6720-4250-85de-80d4899e6200\" from-name=\"Design the no-wizard first-run flow on the canvas\">\nKenneth agreed that an import from File › Import from OrcaSlicer… leaves the open project's printer unchanged.\n\nHe said \"Yes, keep it\" to this on 2026-11-05. The imported printers only join the printer menu. The first launch still selects an imported printer, as it does today. With this, every detail of the menu import is agreed, and the spec section says so.\n</cross-session-message>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:23:31.131Z","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","content":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): allauth-upgrade = local_2c0bf928-2175-4569-9108-2cb6cba1fb77 (idle); use-a-jusprin-syndicate = local_69a34677-cdae-4851-90bb-557cd0ba6d32 (idle); design-the-no-wizard-fir = local_e71c8b0a-6720-4250-85de-80d4899e6200 (idle). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_ca7cba3c-9b94-4c7d-a2bd-83263b3a4832\" from-name=\"btw: tell the coding agent to code up the import menu\">\nBuild the File › Import › \"Import from OrcaSlicer…\" menu item now, reusing what you built for the onboarding import.\n\nKenneth wrote to the design session on 2026-11-05: \"tell the coding agent to code up the import menu. tell it to reuse what was built for the onboarding flow.\"\n\nThe design is fully agreed. It is in the last section of /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md, \"File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer… (after the first launch)\", and on canvas boards orca-import-01 to 05 (version 113). The section also lists what to prove; the two-runs check is the important one.\n\nReuse rather than rebuild:\n- Detection: detect_orca_profiles(), including the ticked and selected printers you added.\n- The import: import_orca_files() and plan_orca_import, plus the ticked-printer install.\n- The result lines: import_result_lines() and Retry.\n- The folder picker: choose_orca_folder().\n- The list and result UI: Onboarding.tsx 07 and 17. Factor the list and the result into shared components so the dialog and the onboarding screens render the same markup. Don't copy them.\n\nWhat differs from onboarding:\n- It's a dialog over the current screen, with no carried \"Signed in\" line, no Start fresh and no Back.\n- Printers JusPrin already has are listed as \"Already in JusPrin\" and skipped: same name and same inherits. This replaces today's \"(Orca copy)\" duplicates.\n- It doesn't change the open project's printer.\n- There is a state for nothing new and a state for no folder found.\n- The MainFrame.cpp change is one append_menu_item line in the import_menu block that calls fork code.\n</cross-session-message>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:23:31.134Z","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"local_44bb8ebc-637f-4344-b9ce-5b49d9e98486\" from-name=\"Fix app freeze after clicking Import on OrcaSlicer printers step\">\nKenneth asked me to hand you the fix for the ~49 s freeze when Import is clicked on \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\" (his words: \"Hand to that session\"). You're rewriting that code now in Home/OrcaImporter.cpp, so I won't touch it.\n\nWhat happened: Kenneth ran your worktree's build (pid 14154, --datadir /tmp/JusPrinStg/JusPrin2). His log, /tmp/JusPrinStg/JusPrin2/log/debug_Thu_Nov_05_17_18_01_14154.log.0, shows the click at 17:24:40.9 and the UI back at about 17:25:29.6. All of it ran on the main thread, inside the onboarding_import handler.\n\nCause: the import calls SetupCommands::install_and_select_printer 7 times, once per printer. In your current code that is the base-profile loop in OrcaImporter::import_files (Creality Ender-3 V2 Neo, Elegoo Neptune 3 Pro, Qidi X-Plus 4) plus OrcaImporter::install_ticked (Kobra 3, A1 mini, K1C, Generic Klipper, P1S). Each call runs PresetBundle::apply_vendor_config, which copies that vendor's bundle and calls load_presets: a full reload of all printer, filament and process profiles. The reloads took 2.7, 2.8, 2.9, 3.1, 5.0, 5.0, 6.0 and 5.1 s, growing as more vendors were loaded. Selecting, naming and refreshing the sidebar added 1.5–2.5 s between installs. import_presets itself took about 0.1 s.\n\nSuggested fix (Kenneth hasn't approved it yet):\n1. Collect every needed (vendor, model, nozzle): the missing bases plus the ticked printers. Install them with ONE apply_vendor_config call. It takes the whole vendor → models → nozzles map, the way Orca's WebGuideDialog wizard does. Then select each printer with find_system_preset_by_model_and_variant + Tab::select_preset, and name it, with no further reload. Expected result: one reload of about 6 s instead of seven totalling about 33 s.\n2. Before the work starts, push a busy \"Importing…\" state to the page, then run the import on the next event-loop turn (CallAfter), so the click visibly does something.\nI'd keep the reload on the UI thread: Orca's sidebar and tabs read PresetBundle all the time.\n\nFull notes: /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_945d7f03-2ea6-4de5-9da6-785e89f1e213/orca-import-freeze-findings.md\n</cross-session-message>"}
{"parentUuid":"b1cc701b-80a9-46e9-9b52-3a8818d6d0eb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5d2f27f1-fa62-43b4-be21-677463a75f5c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): allauth-upgrade = local_2c0bf928-2175-4569-9108-2cb6cba1fb77 (idle); use-a-jusprin-syndicate = local_69a34677-cdae-4851-90bb-557cd0ba6d32 (idle); design-the-no-wizard-fir = local_e71c8b0a-6720-4250-85de-80d4899e6200 (idle). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_e71c8b0a-6720-4250-85de-80d4899e6200\" from-name=\"Design the no-wizard first-run flow on the canvas\">\nKenneth agreed that the File › Import from OrcaSlicer… dialog skips printers JusPrin already has.\n\nHe said \"Yes, keep it\" to that on 2026-11-05, and the spec section is updated. Printers count as already in JusPrin when a preset has the same name and the same inherits. They show as \"Already in JusPrin\" and are not copied again as \"(Orca copy)\".\n\nOne detail is still a proposal he hasn't answered: an import from the menu leaves the open project's printer unchanged. Build it that way unless he says otherwise.\n</cross-session-message>"},"uuid":"764d574d-2570-4a36-9226-4494ff52316b","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:23:31.143Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"sdk","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":57,"turnIndex":86},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
