{"parentUuid":"7d28a660-277f-42ae-9571-eeedda2a37fd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgksyR6UoMfQbN9tuw3AV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1689,"cache_read_input_tokens":282999,"output_tokens":794,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":157},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1689,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":794,"cache_read_input_tokens":282999,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1689,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1689},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1775,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgksyQYysaCQxqBLHJ69w","requestRef":"8bd91156-5295-4be5-a3c6-f605d8731765","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"01902fc7-79ae-4a24-af88-0ab7046dc407","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:23:54.555Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"01902fc7-79ae-4a24-af88-0ab7046dc407","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgksyR6UoMfQbN9tuw3AV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No code change is needed: commit ee3a17e64b on `claude/orca-import-menu` already skips presets JusPrin already has, by the rule Kenneth agreed to. A preset counts as already there when JusPrin has one with the same name, or an \"(Orca copy)\" of it, and the same base. The app showed that skip on a second run.\n\nThe base is compared under the name JusPrin actually loaded it as. OrcaSlicer saves \"Elegoo Generic ABS - Copy\" based on \"Generic ABS @System\", because JusPrin doesn't have \"Elegoo Generic ABS\". Without that comparison, every run would have imported that filament again as \"(Orca copy)\".\n\nOne case departs from \"an import from the menu leaves the open project's printer unchanged\". That's the \"Generic printer\" the first launch installs when someone picks no printer. If it's still selected, the menu import switches to OrcaSlicer's selected printer, the way the first launch does. Every other printer stays selected; I tested this with Bambu Lab P1S selected.\n\nHere's why I made the exception. Once a person has a printer of their own, Home hides the \"Generic printer\" card and its text names a real printer, for example \"JusPrin slices it for your Anycubic Kobra 3\". If the stand-in stayed selected, the next model opened would still slice for the hidden generic printer. When the switch happens, the result screen says so: \"JusPrin now uses Bambu Lab P1S in place of the generic printer.\"\n\nDecision needed: should the menu import still swap out that stand-in printer, or keep every selected printer, the stand-in included? Swapping keeps Home's text true, and it's what the code does now. Keeping it follows the stated rule with no exception, but Home would then name a printer the next model doesn't slice for. My pick is to keep the swap. Undoing it is a few lines in `OrcaImportWindow::import()` plus one sentence on the result screen. Should the swap stay?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1689,"cache_read_input_tokens":282999,"output_tokens":794,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":157},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1689,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":794,"cache_read_input_tokens":282999,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1689,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1689},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgksyQYysaCQxqBLHJ69w","requestRef":"8bd91156-5295-4be5-a3c6-f605d8731765","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ce05338d-09f4-4ff4-b794-8f379903c2c6","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:24:00.646Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"ce05338d-09f4-4ff4-b794-8f379903c2c6","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"stop_hook_summary","hookCount":4,"hookInfos":[{"command":"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code stop'","durationMs":21563},{"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-stop.sh","durationMs":26},{"command":"callback"},{"command":"callback"}],"hookErrors":[],"hookAdditionalContext":[],"preventedContinuation":false,"stopReason":"","hasOutput":false,"level":"suggestion","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:24:22.233Z","uuid":"ea534362-5d53-43d2-bb7d-f83b38eb3017","toolUseID":"73d712a4-2890-49fd-adee-acfc2e9afa91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
