{"parentUuid":"ea534362-5d53-43d2-bb7d-f83b38eb3017","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ec2ae2d8-77f9-48b5-8da0-170b3d96d169","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): allauth-upgrade = local_2c0bf928-2175-4569-9108-2cb6cba1fb77 (idle); use-a-jusprin-syndicate = local_69a34677-cdae-4851-90bb-557cd0ba6d32 (idle); design-the-no-wizard-fir = local_e71c8b0a-6720-4250-85de-80d4899e6200 (idle). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_e71c8b0a-6720-4250-85de-80d4899e6200\" from-name=\"Design the no-wizard first-run flow on the canvas\">\nKenneth agreed that an import from File › Import from OrcaSlicer… leaves the open project's printer unchanged.\n\nHe said \"Yes, keep it\" to this on 2026-11-05. The imported printers only join the printer menu. The first launch still selects an imported printer, as it does today. With this, every detail of the menu import is agreed, and the spec section says so.\n</cross-session-message>\n<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): allauth-upgrade = local_2c0bf928-2175-4569-9108-2cb6cba1fb77 (idle); use-a-jusprin-syndicate = local_69a34677-cdae-4851-90bb-557cd0ba6d32 (idle); design-the-no-wizard-fir = local_e71c8b0a-6720-4250-85de-80d4899e6200 (idle). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_ca7cba3c-9b94-4c7d-a2bd-83263b3a4832\" from-name=\"btw: tell the coding agent to code up the import menu\">\nBuild the File › Import › \"Import from OrcaSlicer…\" menu item now, reusing what you built for the onboarding import.\n\nKenneth wrote to the design session on 2026-11-05: \"tell the coding agent to code up the import menu. tell it to reuse what was built for the onboarding flow.\"\n\nThe design is fully agreed. It is in the last section of /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md, \"File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer… (after the first launch)\", and on canvas boards orca-import-01 to 05 (version 113). The section also lists what to prove; the two-runs check is the important one.\n\nReuse rather than rebuild:\n- Detection: detect_orca_profiles(), including the ticked and selected printers you added.\n- The import: import_orca_files() and plan_orca_import, plus the ticked-printer install.\n- The result lines: import_result_lines() and Retry.\n- The folder picker: choose_orca_folder().\n- The list and result UI: Onboarding.tsx 07 and 17. Factor the list and the result into shared components so the dialog and the onboarding screens render the same markup. Don't copy them.\n\nWhat differs from onboarding:\n- It's a dialog over the current screen, with no carried \"Signed in\" line, no Start fresh and no Back.\n- Printers JusPrin already has are listed as \"Already in JusPrin\" and skipped: same name and same inherits. This replaces today's \"(Orca copy)\" duplicates.\n- It doesn't change the open project's printer.\n- There is a state for nothing new and a state for no folder found.\n- The MainFrame.cpp change is one append_menu_item line in the import_menu block that calls fork code.\n</cross-session-message>"},"uuid":"0e3a1c48-3399-470a-b329-4ebea58d9f9c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:24:22.251Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"sdk","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":57,"turnIndex":87},"mergedSendUuids":["4a733cac-f452-4921-af38-94e05b2b7437"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
