{"parentUuid":"5a0da26a-5dac-406a-9ba0-20b2a0214d3a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkt3AuZAJzmhLgKHgmUJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013uGmH8wAA4MFkYkqMNKbyk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"F=/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md; n=$(grep -n \"Import from OrcaSlicer… (after the first launch)\" $F | head -1 | cut -d: -f1); sed -n \"$n,\\$p\" $F","description":"Read the menu import section of the spec"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2071,"cache_read_input_tokens":284688,"output_tokens":1104,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":683},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2071,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1104,"cache_read_input_tokens":284688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2071,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2071},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013uGmH8wAA4MFkYkqMNKbyk":{"command":"F=/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md; n=$(grep -n \"Import from OrcaSlicer… (after the first launch)\" $F | head -1 | cut -d: -f1); sed -n \"$n,\\$p\" $F","description":"Read the menu import section of the spec"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgkt3AXzBWDRk1BQkBSFY","requestRef":"2d0162a1-16e1-4540-80e5-bab9f37f73ba","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"708311d1-f156-42a3-a007-6a0d2264a65e","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:24:53.368Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"708311d1-f156-42a3-a007-6a0d2264a65e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ec2ae2d8-77f9-48b5-8da0-170b3d96d169","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013uGmH8wAA4MFkYkqMNKbyk","type":"tool_result","content":"## File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer… (after the first launch)\n\nKenneth, 2026-11-05: \"I want to add a menu item under \"File\" to let user import orcaslicer profiles\", the item reading \"Import from OrcaSlicer\", and \"Yes, draw it\". Boards `orca-import-01` to `05` on the canvas (version 111), in the row \"Later, from the File menu\" under Home.\n\n- **01. The menu item.** \"Import from OrcaSlicer…\" is the last item in File › Import, after OrcaSlicer's own \"Import Configs…\" (`MainFrame.cpp`, the `import_menu` block). MainFrame.cpp is an OrcaSlicer file, so add one `append_menu_item` line that calls into fork code, and follow `fork-stewardship.md`.\n- **02. The dialog,** over whatever screen is open. It has a title row \"Import from OrcaSlicer\" with a close button. The lead says \"JusPrin found 2 printers in OrcaSlicer that it doesn't have yet. JusPrin copies them with their filaments, settings and printer connections. OrcaSlicer keeps its own copy.\" Below that is the same list as 07, then the folder path with \"Choose another folder…\". The buttons are Cancel and \"Import N printers\". It uses the same detection as 07, including ticked and selected printers. It has none of the first-launch parts: no carried line, no Start fresh, no Back.\n- **03. The result.** Title \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\", then \"They are in the printer menu. The printer this project uses didn't change. OrcaSlicer's own files were not changed.\" Below that are the same lines as 17 and the filament count, then Done.\n- **04. Nothing new.** Every printer is listed as \"Already in JusPrin\". The lead says \"Every printer in this OrcaSlicer folder is already in JusPrin, so there is nothing to import.\" The only buttons are \"Choose another folder…\" and Close.\n- **05. No folder found.** \"JusPrin didn't find OrcaSlicer's folder on this computer. If OrcaSlicer keeps its settings somewhere else, choose that folder.\" It shows the path it looked in, with Cancel and \"Choose the folder…\".\n\nAgreed by Kenneth on 2026-11-05 (\"Yes, keep it\"):\n- Printers JusPrin already has show as \"Already in JusPrin\" and are skipped, along with their filaments and processes. Today `plan_orca_import` (`Home/OrcaImport.cpp`) saves a second copy, \"… (Orca copy)\", of any preset whose name JusPrin already has, so a second run would double everything. A preset counts as \"already in JusPrin\" when JusPrin has a preset with the same name and the same `inherits`. A same-named preset with different settings still imports as \"(Orca copy)\", as today.\n- Agreed the same day (\"Yes, keep it\"): the import from the menu doesn't change the open project's printer. It only adds printers to the printer menu. The first launch still selects one, as it does today.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6015d8de-f6f9-489b-96b2-06bcc1c8b352","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:24:53.621Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer… (after the first launch)\n\nKenneth, 2026-11-05: \"I want to add a menu item under \"File\" to let user import orcaslicer profiles\", the item reading \"Import from OrcaSlicer\", and \"Yes, draw it\". Boards `orca-import-01` to `05` on the canvas (version 111), in the row \"Later, from the File menu\" under Home.\n\n- **01. The menu item.** \"Import from OrcaSlicer…\" is the last item in File › Import, after OrcaSlicer's own \"Import Configs…\" (`MainFrame.cpp`, the `import_menu` block). MainFrame.cpp is an OrcaSlicer file, so add one `append_menu_item` line that calls into fork code, and follow `fork-stewardship.md`.\n- **02. The dialog,** over whatever screen is open. It has a title row \"Import from OrcaSlicer\" with a close button. The lead says \"JusPrin found 2 printers in OrcaSlicer that it doesn't have yet. JusPrin copies them with their filaments, settings and printer connections. OrcaSlicer keeps its own copy.\" Below that is the same list as 07, then the folder path with \"Choose another folder…\". The buttons are Cancel and \"Import N printers\". It uses the same detection as 07, including ticked and selected printers. It has none of the first-launch parts: no carried line, no Start fresh, no Back.\n- **03. The result.** Title \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\", then \"They are in the printer menu. The printer this project uses didn't change. OrcaSlicer's own files were not changed.\" Below that are the same lines as 17 and the filament count, then Done.\n- **04. Nothing new.** Every printer is listed as \"Already in JusPrin\". The lead says \"Every printer in this OrcaSlicer folder is already in JusPrin, so there is nothing to import.\" The only buttons are \"Choose another folder…\" and Close.\n- **05. No folder found.** \"JusPrin didn't find OrcaSlicer's folder on this computer. If OrcaSlicer keeps its settings somewhere else, choose that folder.\" It shows the path it looked in, with Cancel and \"Choose the folder…\".\n\nAgreed by Kenneth on 2026-11-05 (\"Yes, keep it\"):\n- Printers JusPrin already has show as \"Already in JusPrin\" and are skipped, along with their filaments and processes. Today `plan_orca_import` (`Home/OrcaImport.cpp`) saves a second copy, \"… (Orca copy)\", of any preset whose name JusPrin already has, so a second run would double everything. A preset counts as \"already in JusPrin\" when JusPrin has a preset with the same name and the same `inherits`. A same-named preset with different settings still imports as \"(Orca copy)\", as today.\n- Agreed the same day (\"Yes, keep it\"): the import from the menu doesn't change the open project's printer. It only adds printers to the printer menu. The first launch still selects one, as it does today.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"708311d1-f156-42a3-a007-6a0d2264a65e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"6015d8de-f6f9-489b-96b2-06bcc1c8b352","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<cross-session-message from=\"local_44bb8ebc-637f-4344-b9ce-5b49d9e98486\" from-name=\"Fix app freeze after clicking Import on OrcaSlicer printers step\">\nKenneth asked me to hand you the fix for the ~49 s freeze when Import is clicked on \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\" (his words: \"Hand to that session\"). You're rewriting that code now in Home/OrcaImporter.cpp, so I won't touch it.\n\nWhat happened: Kenneth ran your worktree's build (pid 14154, --datadir /tmp/JusPrinStg/JusPrin2). His log, /tmp/JusPrinStg/JusPrin2/log/debug_Thu_Nov_05_17_18_01_14154.log.0, shows the click at 17:24:40.9 and the UI back at about 17:25:29.6. All of it ran on the main thread, inside the onboarding_import handler.\n\nCause: the import calls SetupCommands::install_and_select_printer 7 times, once per printer. In your current code that is the base-profile loop in OrcaImporter::import_files (Creality Ender-3 V2 Neo, Elegoo Neptune 3 Pro, Qidi X-Plus 4) plus OrcaImporter::install_ticked (Kobra 3, A1 mini, K1C, Generic Klipper, P1S). Each call runs PresetBundle::apply_vendor_config, which copies that vendor's bundle and calls load_presets: a full reload of all printer, filament and process profiles. The reloads took 2.7, 2.8, 2.9, 3.1, 5.0, 5.0, 6.0 and 5.1 s, growing as more vendors were loaded. Selecting, naming and refreshing the sidebar added 1.5–2.5 s between installs. import_presets itself took about 0.1 s.\n\nSuggested fix (Kenneth hasn't approved it yet):\n1. Collect every needed (vendor, model, nozzle): the missing bases plus the ticked printers. Install them with ONE apply_vendor_config call. It takes the whole vendor → models → nozzles map, the way Orca's WebGuideDialog wizard does. Then select each printer with find_system_preset_by_model_and_variant + Tab::select_preset, and name it, with no further reload. Expected result: one reload of about 6 s instead of seven totalling about 33 s.\n2. Before the work starts, push a busy \"Importing…\" state to the page, then run the import on the next event-loop turn (CallAfter), so the click visibly does something.\nI'd keep the reload on the UI thread: Orca's sidebar and tabs read PresetBundle all the time.\n\nFull notes: /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_945d7f03-2ea6-4de5-9da6-785e89f1e213/orca-import-freeze-findings.md\n</cross-session-message>","source_uuid":"bdec3db2-64ea-44e2-a499-9629bf8b039a","delivery_id":"5504b2f2-9549-4e04-831b-be968b36899c","commandMode":"prompt","origin":{"kind":"peer","from":"local_44bb8ebc-637f-4344-b9ce-5b49d9e98486","name":"Fix app freeze after clicking Import on OrcaSlicer printers step","body":"Kenneth asked me to hand you the fix for the ~49 s freeze when Import is clicked on \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\" (his words: \"Hand to that session\"). You're rewriting that code now in Home/OrcaImporter.cpp, so I won't touch it.\n\nWhat happened: Kenneth ran your worktree's build (pid 14154, --datadir /tmp/JusPrinStg/JusPrin2). His log, /tmp/JusPrinStg/JusPrin2/log/debug_Thu_Nov_05_17_18_01_14154.log.0, shows the click at 17:24:40.9 and the UI back at about 17:25:29.6. All of it ran on the main thread, inside the onboarding_import handler.\n\nCause: the import calls SetupCommands::install_and_select_printer 7 times, once per printer. In your current code that is the base-profile loop in OrcaImporter::import_files (Creality Ender-3 V2 Neo, Elegoo Neptune 3 Pro, Qidi X-Plus 4) plus OrcaImporter::install_ticked (Kobra 3, A1 mini, K1C, Generic Klipper, P1S). Each call runs PresetBundle::apply_vendor_config, which copies that vendor's bundle and calls load_presets: a full reload of all printer, filament and process profiles. The reloads took 2.7, 2.8, 2.9, 3.1, 5.0, 5.0, 6.0 and 5.1 s, growing as more vendors were loaded. Selecting, naming and refreshing the sidebar added 1.5–2.5 s between installs. import_presets itself took about 0.1 s.\n\nSuggested fix (Kenneth hasn't approved it yet):\n1. Collect every needed (vendor, model, nozzle): the missing bases plus the ticked printers. Install them with ONE apply_vendor_config call. It takes the whole vendor → models → nozzles map, the way Orca's WebGuideDialog wizard does. Then select each printer with find_system_preset_by_model_and_variant + Tab::select_preset, and name it, with no further reload. Expected result: one reload of about 6 s instead of seven totalling about 33 s.\n2. Before the work starts, push a busy \"Importing…\" state to the page, then run the import on the next event-loop turn (CallAfter), so the click visibly does something.\nI'd keep the reload on the UI thread: Orca's sidebar and tabs read PresetBundle all the time.\n\nFull notes: /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_945d7f03-2ea6-4de5-9da6-785e89f1e213/orca-import-freeze-findings.md","hostInjected":true,"fromMode":"bypass"},"timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:23:31.134Z","isMeta":true,"reminderId":"646ac3014a5af76b"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a8e9953a-b790-4f8c-ad35-3d216d91b31f","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:23:31.134Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder id=\"646ac3014a5af76b\">\nAnother Claude session sent a message while you were working:\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_44bb8ebc-637f-4344-b9ce-5b49d9e98486\" from-name=\"Fix app freeze after clicking Import on OrcaSlicer printers step\">\nKenneth asked me to hand you the fix for the ~49 s freeze when Import is clicked on \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\" (his words: \"Hand to that session\"). You're rewriting that code now in Home/OrcaImporter.cpp, so I won't touch it.\n\nWhat happened: Kenneth ran your worktree's build (pid 14154, --datadir /tmp/JusPrinStg/JusPrin2). His log, /tmp/JusPrinStg/JusPrin2/log/debug_Thu_Nov_05_17_18_01_14154.log.0, shows the click at 17:24:40.9 and the UI back at about 17:25:29.6. All of it ran on the main thr