{"parentUuid":"349d0c96-79e3-4aa2-8bcd-e25bc75fab9a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"auto_mode","autoModeConsentFlow":false,"finishExposedWork":false,"bashFirst":true,"bashFirstSteer":"relaxed","steerOnly":true,"bypass":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"760867a3-2553-4a53-b839-8b4a47d147e9","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:32:22.141Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nWhile bypass permissions mode is active:\n\nYou can do much of your work through the Bash tool when it is the simpler route: read files with cat, head, or sed -n, search with grep and find, and make small, mechanical file changes with sed, heredocs, or short scripts instead of the dedicated Read, Edit, or Write tools. The choice is yours: prefer Edit or Write when a shell edit would be fragile, such as exact or multi-line replacements, or sed/awk flags that differ between GNU and BSD/macOS.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
