{"parentUuid":"17e68270-9f47-4e24-b59b-834a6cf286f7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkvJACYnsPV9X4dQyzpG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DwpwVysm1B7GEV4rEjarP6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory && cat drive-app-with-posted-key-events.md scratch-app-driving-traps.md | head -80","description":"Read notes on driving the app while the screen is locked"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":270,"cache_read_input_tokens":198576,"output_tokens":272,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":85},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":270,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":272,"cache_read_input_tokens":198576,"cache_creation_input_tokens":270,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":270},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DwpwVysm1B7GEV4rEjarP6":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory && cat drive-app-with-posted-key-events.md scratch-app-driving-traps.md | head -80","description":"Read notes on driving the app while the screen is locked"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgkvJ9vRTaX19WnrhCw78","requestRef":"f39c59e9-8da2-46f6-824d-362ea19be315","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"computer-use","attributionMcpTool":"app_menu","type":"assistant","uuid":"80f2f454-931f-49bc-8fc8-d488df961f2c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:54:24.962Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/build/arm64","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"80f2f454-931f-49bc-8fc8-d488df961f2c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e2213f06-b568-4154-874a-1f58f6fdb9a9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DwpwVysm1B7GEV4rEjarP6","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: drive-app-with-posted-key-events\ndescription: \"Drive the built JusPrin app headlessly (even with the screen locked) by posting CGEvents to its pid with a tiny Swift tool; keys work, mouse clicks do not, and the send dialog is reachable by keyboard.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 6b96dccc-1cb4-4f72-9de4-3ecee4b28e74\n  modified: 2026-09-08T05:58:16.222Z\n---\n\nWhen the Mac screen is locked (`ioreg -n Root -d1 | grep CGSSessionScreenIsLocked`), the computer-use MCP request is auto-denied, `screencapture` fails, and System Events sees zero windows. Key events still reach the app: a 15-line Swift program calling `CGEvent(keyboardEventSource:virtualKey:keyDown:).postToPid(pid)` (compile with `swiftc`) made the app slice on Cmd+R (keycode 15) and open the send dialog on Cmd+Shift+G (keycode 5). Mouse events posted the same way did nothing, even with the window number set on the event.\n\nInside `PrintHostSendDialog` (Orca `MsgDialog`), focus starts in the filename field; Tab (48) moves to the \"Upload\" button, Right (124) to \"Upload and Print\", Space (49) presses it, because Orca's custom `Button` handles Space/Return and arrow navigation itself. Return alone triggers plain \"Upload\" (the affirmative id), not print.\n\n`CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo` still lists the app's on-screen windows with bounds while locked, which tells you when a modal dialog is open (a small layer-0 window appears) and when it closed.\n\n**Why:** On 2026-09-07 the end-to-end proof of the fake Moonraker printer needed the Print button pressed while the screen was locked; this was the only working path.\n\n**How to apply:** Confirm the target pid first (`pgrep -f <copy>.app/Contents/MacOS`) so keys never go to another session's instance. Watch the app's own `--datadir` `log/debug_*.log` for effects (use `/usr/bin/grep -a`; the default `grep` is ugrep, which treats `\\|` literally and may skip the log as binary). See [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]] and [[fake-moonraker-printer-sim]].\n---\nname: scratch-app-driving-traps\ndescription: \"Five traps met driving a scratch copy of the built app without screen control (2026-11-04): in-place binary copy gets SIGKILL, Home drops bridge messages while hidden, header popups need a posted NSEvent, lldb std::string args, wx Wrap reuse.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: dea8379c-b02c-43a2-a254-4c2259672439\n  modified: 2026-11-04T18:59:38.548Z\n---\n\nMet while verifying print-host printer window fixes on the scratch `.app` (see [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[open-file-in-app-without-screen-control]]).\n\n- **Copy a new build into a `.app` with `rm` then `cp`.** `cp` over the existing signed binary keeps the inode; the kernel kills the launch at once (exit 137, nothing logged).\n- **A launch from a plain Bash call dies when the call ends.** Start the app with `run_in_background: true` and `exec`.\n- **Home ignores bridge messages while the main window shows a project.** A queued `launch_monitor` through `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` is sent by the page and silently dropped; switch to Home first (`m_tabpanel->SetSelection(0)` via lldb).\n- **Background `app_click` does not reach the header's popup menus** (they are not listed as windows). Post the click into the app's queue with lldb: `expr -l objc -- @import AppKit`, then `NSEvent mouseEventWithType:NSEventTypeLeftMouseDown/Up location:NSMakePoint(x, y-from-popup-bottom) ... windowNumber:[popup windowNumber]` and `[NSApp postEvent:atStart:NO]`. Render the popup with `cacheDisplayInRect:` on its contentView ([[capture-mac-popups-for-platform-diff]]).\n- **lldb cannot build `std::string` args.** This libc++ uses the alternate short-string layout: a 24-byte char array with the text at offset 0 and its length in byte 23 (≤ 22 chars), passed as `*(std::string*)buf`.\n- **wx `wxStaticText::Wrap()` (Orca's wx) skips a width it already wrapped at and keeps the first text it wrapped**, so SetLabel + Wrap on a reused label comes back unwrapped. Use a fresh label.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"92aa5256-5b73-4ca8-a44b-69fa9ff092bd","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:54:25.024Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: drive-app-with-posted-key-events\ndescription: \"Drive the built JusPrin app headlessly (even with the screen locked) by posting CGEvents to its pid with a tiny Swift tool; keys work, mouse clicks do not, and the send dialog is reachable by keyboard.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 6b96dccc-1cb4-4f72-9de4-3ecee4b28e74\n  modified: 2026-09-08T05:58:16.222Z\n---\n\nWhen the Mac screen is locked (`ioreg -n Root -d1 | grep CGSSessionScreenIsLocked`), the computer-use MCP request is auto-denied, `screencapture` fails, and System Events sees zero windows. Key events still reach the app: a 15-line Swift program calling `CGEvent(keyboardEventSource:virtualKey:keyDown:).postToPid(pid)` (compile with `swiftc`) made the app slice on Cmd+R (keycode 15) and open the send dialog on Cmd+Shift+G (keycode 5). Mouse events posted the same way did nothing, even with the window number set on the event.\n\nInside `PrintHostSendDialog` (Orca `MsgDialog`), focus starts in the filename field; Tab (48) moves to the \"Upload\" button, Right (124) to \"Upload and Print\", Space (49) presses it, because Orca's custom `Button` handles Space/Return and arrow navigation itself. Return alone triggers plain \"Upload\" (the affirmative id), not print.\n\n`CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo` still lists the app's on-screen windows with bounds while locked, which tells you when a modal dialog is open (a small layer-0 window appears) and when it closed.\n\n**Why:** On 2026-09-07 the end-to-end proof of the fake Moonraker printer needed the Print button pressed while the screen was locked; this was the only working path.\n\n**How to apply:** Confirm the target pid first (`pgrep -f <copy>.app/Contents/MacOS`) so keys never go to another session's instance. Watch the app's own `--datadir` `log/debug_*.log` for effects (use `/usr/bin/grep -a`; the default `grep` is ugrep, which treats `\\|` literally and may skip the log as binary). See [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]] and [[fake-moonraker-printer-sim]].\n---\nname: scratch-app-driving-traps\ndescription: \"Five traps met driving a scratch copy of the built app without screen control (2026-11-04): in-place binary copy gets SIGKILL, Home drops bridge messages while hidden, header popups need a posted NSEvent, lldb std::string args, wx Wrap reuse.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: dea8379c-b02c-43a2-a254-4c2259672439\n  modified: 2026-11-04T18:59:38.548Z\n---\n\nMet while verifying print-host printer window fixes on the scratch `.app` (see [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]], [[open-file-in-app-without-screen-control]]).\n\n- **Copy a new build into a `.app` with `rm` then `cp`.** `cp` over the existing signed binary keeps the inode; the kernel kills the launch at once (exit 137, nothing logged).\n- **A launch from a plain Bash call dies when the call ends.** Start the app with `run_in_background: true` and `exec`.\n- **Home ignores bridge messages while the main window shows a project.** A queued `launch_monitor` through `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` is sent by the page and silently dropped; switch to Home first (`m_tabpanel->SetSelection(0)` via lldb).\n- **Background `app_click` does not reach the header's popup menus** (they are not listed as windows). Post the click into the app's queue with lldb: `expr -l objc -- @import AppKit`, then `NSEvent mouseEventWithType:NSEventTypeLeftMouseDown/Up location:NSMakePoint(x, y-from-popup-bottom) ... windowNumber:[popup windowNumber]` and `[NSApp postEvent:atStart:NO]`. Render the popup with `cacheDisplayInRect:` on its contentView ([[capture-mac-popups-for-platform-diff]]).\n- **lldb cannot build `std::string` args.** This libc++ uses the alternate short-string layout: a 24-byte char array with the text at offset 0 and its length in byte 23 (≤ 22 chars), passed as `*(std::string*)buf`.\n- **wx `wxStaticText::Wrap()` (Orca's wx) skips a width it already wrapped at and keeps the first text it wrapped**, so SetLabel + Wrap on a reused label comes back unwrapped. Use a fresh label.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"80f2f454-931f-49bc-8fc8-d488df961f2c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
