{"parentUuid":"55e46dcc-6dc6-4e93-872d-d5767b70ddf2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgky9My5HtSD8UfBWyxUM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FbTqQ2haqJwst23sMPBWR1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/OrcaImportApp.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImport.test.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImport.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/styles.css src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaHomeBackend.hpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaImportWindow.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaImportWindow.hpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaImporter.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaImporter.hpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/App.test.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/styles.css src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/SetupCommands.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/SetupCommands.hpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImportLists.css src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImportLists.styles.test.ts src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImportLists.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/WebShared/afterPaint.ts && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nOrcaSlicer import: install every needed profile in one reload, share the list markup, and show \"Importing…\" before the work\n\nImporting OrcaSlicer's printers froze the app for close to a minute,\non the first launch's Printers step and from File › Import › Import from\nOrcaSlicer…. Each printer that needed a profile installed reloaded every\npreset, seven reloads for the eight printers in the test folder, and the\n\"Importing…\" label never painted because the work ran inside the click's\nmessage.\n\n- SetupCommands::install_printer_profiles installs every vendor, model\n  and nozzle the import needs with one PresetBundle::apply_vendor_config,\n  and puts the previous vendors, filaments and printer back if it fails.\n  OrcaImporter::bring calls it once, then imports the files and names the\n  ticked printers without another reload. install_and_select_printer\n  shares the snapshot and restore code.\n- Both pages set \"Importing…\" and send the import message only after the\n  browser has painted it (WebShared/afterPaint.ts). Every button on the\n  step is disabled meanwhile; the host's next state ends it.\n- The printer list and the result lines are one component,\n  AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImportLists.tsx with its own stylesheet,\n  drawn by the dialog and by the first launch's Printers step. The\n  duplicated rules in both pages' stylesheets are gone, and a guard test\n  checks the shared stylesheet uses only variables both pages define.\n- The dialog gets \"Retry failed items\", using the same retry as the\n  first launch (moved into OrcaImporter, with the folder picker).\n- The menu import no longer swaps the generic stand-in printer for an\n  imported one: Kenneth decided on 2026-11-05 that it only adds printers\n  to the printer menu and leaves the project's printer, filaments and\n  process as they were. The result always says the project's printer\n  didn't change.\n\nTested: jusprin_tests (166 cases), AgentUI vitest (678), HomeUI vitest\n(155), tsc on both pages. In the built app on copies of an OrcaSlicer\nfolder with 8 printers, with the screen locked: the menu import did one\nfull preset reload instead of seven and took 22 s instead of about 60 s,\nkept \"Generic printer\" and the project's process and filament selected,\nand a second run showed \"nothing new\" with no \"(Orca copy)\" files. The\nfirst-launch import, old and new builds back to back on the same fresh\nfolder, took 226 s with the old code and 93 s with the new. Both pages\nshowed \"Importing…\" with the other buttons disabled before the import\nbegan. The no-folder screen was unchanged.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1; git status --short","description":"Commit the import speed-up and shared components"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":471,"cache_read_input_tokens":278542,"output_tokens":1836,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":38},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":471,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1836,"cache_read_input_tokens":278542,"cache_creation_input_tokens":471,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":471},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FbTqQ2haqJwst23sMPBWR1":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35 && git add src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/OrcaImportApp.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImport.test.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImport.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/styles.css src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaHomeBackend.hpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaImportWindow.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaImportWindow.hpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaImporter.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaImporter.hpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/App.test.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/HomeUI/src/styles.css src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/SetupCommands.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/SetupCommands.hpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImportLists.css src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImportLists.styles.test.ts src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImportLists.tsx src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/WebShared/afterPaint.ts && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nOrcaSlicer import: install every needed profile in one reload, share the list markup, and show \"Importing…\" before the work\n\nImporting OrcaSlicer's printers froze the app for close to a minute,\non the first launch's Printers step and from File › Import › Import from\nOrcaSlicer…. Each printer that needed a profile installed reloaded every\npreset, seven reloads for the eight printers in the test folder, and the\n\"Importing…\" label never painted because the work ran inside the click's\nmessage.\n\n- SetupCommands::install_printer_profiles installs every vendor, model\n  and nozzle the import needs with one PresetBundle::apply_vendor_config,\n  and puts the previous vendors, filaments and printer back if it fails.\n  OrcaImporter::bring calls it once, then imports the files and names the\n  ticked printers without another reload. install_and_select_printer\n  shares the snapshot and restore code.\n- Both pages set \"Importing…\" and send the import message only after the\n  browser has painted it (WebShared/afterPaint.ts). Every button on the\n  step is disabled meanwhile; the host's next state ends it.\n- The printer list and the result lines are one component,\n  AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImportLists.tsx with its own stylesheet,\n  drawn by the dialog and by the first launch's Printers step. The\n  duplicated rules in both pages' stylesheets are gone, and a guard test\n  checks the shared stylesheet uses only variables both pages define.\n- The dialog gets \"Retry failed items\", using the same retry as the\n  first launch (moved into OrcaImporter, with the folder picker).\n- The menu import no longer swaps the generic stand-in printer for an\n  imported one: Kenneth decided on 2026-11-05 that it only adds printers\n  to the printer menu and leaves the project's printer, filaments and\n  process as they were. The result always says the project's printer\n  didn't change.\n\nTested: jusprin_tests (166 cases), AgentUI vitest (678), HomeUI vitest\n(155), tsc on both pages. In the built app on copies of an OrcaSlicer\nfolder with 8 printers, with the screen locked: the menu import did one\nfull preset reload instead of seven and took 22 s instead of about 60 s,\nkept \"Generic printer\" and the project's process and filament selected,\nand a second run showed \"nothing new\" with no \"(Orca copy)\" files. The\nfirst-launch import, old and new builds back to back on the same fresh\nfolder, took 226 s with the old code and 93 s with the new. Both pages\nshowed \"Importing…\" with the other buttons disabled before the import\nbegan. The no-folder screen was unchanged.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1; git status --short","description":"Commit the import speed-up and shared components"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01FbTqQ2haqJwst23sMPBWR1":{"cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35"}},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011Cgky9MjC4DQo1T87aeer9","requestRef":"fa1032d4-d9ae-4399-9275-eb7c8196cccc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e83c345f-71e9-484a-8b5d-4f5c8d267289","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:31:57.677Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
