{"parentUuid":"6b6d3780-9877-4162-827c-2e4fea753809","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkyC33cqDc1mCFJwSwop","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014P7V7yc1zUNcVo8ebco2WA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory && cat >> scratch-app-driving-traps.md <<'EOF'\n- **With the screen locked, an instrumented dev page stops polling** (WebKit throttles the hidden page's timers; `document.visibilityState` is \"hidden\"). Run JS in it through lldb instead: walk `[NSApp windows]` → subviews to the `WKWebView` (match its title or `URL`), then `[webview evaluateJavaScript:@\"…\" completionHandler:nil]`; the page can `fetch()` results to the dev server. A menu item without a shortcut: `[[item target] performSelector:[item action] withObject:item afterDelay:0.5]` from lldb, so the modal it opens runs after detach.\n- **A locked screen slows the whole app 2-4×** (2026-11-05: the same first-launch OrcaSlicer import took 46 s unlocked at 15:48, 226 s locked at 19:22, same build and folder). Compare timings only between back-to-back runs under the same conditions, old and new builds side by side.\nEOF\nsed -i '' 's/^description: \"Five traps met driving/description: \"Seven traps met driving/' scratch-app-driving-traps.md; grep -n \"Scratch-app traps\" MEMORY.md | head -2","description":"Add the locked-screen driving lessons to memory"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":577,"cache_read_input_tokens":283254,"output_tokens":726,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":144},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":577,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_to