{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","id":"cf2d585c-cbad-401f-b4b0-6a7ba1f72d6f","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:32:39.615Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"6be4cbcf13bd24f91c1084271e54c66443d4511e9a00e5bc8042b89ce33d2e34","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"0d22645f-8620-4477-9319-5ca378770d25","keep":335,"tail":["d8053432878f0c50387521dd3b279b6ff8be373eeee4b47dfe2e89a4eb41cb03","a05f6a378b7287c0cb5659c2cbcca0cec7931ce696af250938a9cea07f70f655","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",337,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"7c172fb18371754f3405b4b82105764e10f5782e69e970e4b80f0001f6eabee6"}
{"parentUuid":"2b9d7cb7-eb19-4ff0-a602-7fec35498d4f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkyDfYc1x5ftWJ3bNTPW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed as **242a9e73ba** on `claude/orca-import-menu`; not pushed or merged. The OrcaSlicer import no longer reloads every preset once per printer. Both the File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer… dialog and the first launch's Printers step draw one shared printer list and result list, and both show \"Importing…\" before the work starts.\n\n**What was wrong.** Each printer that needed a profile installed reloaded all presets: seven full reloads for the eight printers in my test copy of an OrcaSlicer folder. The work also ran inside the click, so \"Importing…\" never got drawn before the app froze.\n\n**What changed**\n- **One reload:** every vendor, model and nozzle the import needs now goes in with one preset reload. Then each ticked printer is saved under its name with no further reload.\n- **Busy label:** both screens draw \"Importing…\" with every other button disabled, and only then send the import request. The helper for that is `WebShared/afterPaint.ts`.\n- **Shared lists:** the printer list and result lines are one component, `AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImportLists.tsx`, with its own stylesheet. The copies on both pages are deleted. A new test checks the shared stylesheet uses only design variables both pages define.\n- **Retry:** the dialog has \"Retry failed items\", using the same retry code as the first launch.\n- **Project printer:** as you decided, the menu import no longer swaps the stand-in \"Generic printer\" for an imported one. It only adds printers to the printer menu.\n\n**What I tested**\n- The native tests (166), the Agent page tests (678), the Home page tests (155) and the type checks on both pages all pass.\n- **Menu import, in the built app:**\n  - It now takes 22 seconds instead of about 60.\n  - \"Generic printer\" and the project's process and filament stayed selected.\n  - A second run said there was nothing new, with every printer marked \"Already in JusPrin\" and no \"(Orca copy)\" files.\n  - The screen for a computer with no OrcaSlicer folder is unchanged.\n- **First launch:** I built the previous commit too and ran both builds back to back on the same fresh data folder. The old code took 226 seconds, the new code 93.\n\n**Not verified**\n- **Times with the screen unlocked.** The Mac was locked for all of these runs, and a locked screen slows the app two to four times. An identical old-code run took 46 seconds this afternoon with the screen unlocked, so I expect the new first launch to take roughly 20 seconds. I haven't measured it.\n- **Whether \"Importing…\" shows on screen.** With the screen locked I couldn't see the window. I confirmed the label was in place, with the other buttons disabled, before the import began, but I never saw it painted.\n- **Retry in the dialog** was tested only by the page tests, not in the app.\n\n**Still slow.** Most of the remaining time is about 2.6 seconds per ticked printer from the menu, and longer while locked. OrcaSlicer spends it saving each named printer: every save copies the whole preset bundle for its compare dialog. Fixing that means changing upstream OrcaSlicer code, so it should be a separate change.\n\nThe session that handed over the freeze fix no longer exists, so it didn't get this report.\n\nShould I push `claude/orca-import-menu` now, or hold it until you've tried the import with the screen unlocked?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":355,"cache_read_input_tokens":285282,"output_tokens":1118,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":355,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo"