{"parentUuid":"a08ed3d9-684d-431d-90f7-7ef9242a1dbe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm6yY2DczBTZhVpasbH9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y7bZt5XuJdfrGms6QXgZD6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> restore-temp-edits-from-a-copy.md <<'EOF'\n\n**Never `cp -p` the copy back before a build.** 2026-11-05: to build the previous commit for an A/B timing, I swapped in old sources, built, then restored my files with `cp -p`. Their kept 18:28 dates were older than the 19:19 objects, so ninja recompiled nothing: the build folder, the next app copy and a jusprin_tests rerun all held the old code while looking current. Restore with plain `cp` (or `touch` the files), then check the binary holds a string only the new code has before trusting it.\nEOF\nsed -i '' 's/^description: \"After a temporary edit to prove a test fails, restore from a saved copy, never `git checkout <file>` — it also wipes your uncommitted work in that file.\"/description: \"After a temporary edit, restore from a saved copy, never `git checkout <file>` (wipes uncommitted work); and never with `cp -p` before a build (old dates, ninja skips the recompile).\"/' restore-temp-edits-from-a-copy.md; head -3 restore-temp-edits-from-a-copy.md | tail -1; grep -n \"restore-temp-edits\" MEMORY.md","description":"Record the preserved-date rebuild trap in memory"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":857,"cache_read_input_tokens":338967,"output_tokens":530,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":857,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":530,"cache_read_input_tokens":338967,"cache_creation_input_