{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01Fx7UioApoHEkwHCUFqCo1e","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"7911d73c-5552-4877-a943-6a0eba3d7c4d","ownerOrganizationUuid":"68a648b0-98a4-49c7-902b-ff471f8d1d46"}
{"parentUuid":"5e7c305b-24be-449d-990c-afa3af155434","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm7aEyW9zYCXDJaJERJF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed as **37c24299b9** on `claude/orca-import-menu`; not pushed. \"Importing…\" now stays on screen for the whole OrcaSlicer import, on the first launch's Printers step and in the File › Import window.\n\n**The fix.** The page used to send the import request one frame after the click. The page had drawn \"Importing…\" by then, but the app hadn't yet put that frame on screen, and the import blocked it. The page now waits one more frame plus 50 milliseconds before sending.\n\n**What I saw on screen**, with full-screen control, in screenshots taken 1 to 15 seconds after clicking, all while the import was running:\n- **First-launch step:** a greyed \"Importing…\" button, with Start fresh and Back disabled.\n- **Menu window:** \"Importing…\" on the Import button.\n- Both pages' tests pass (678 and 155).\n\n**Timings**, screen unlocked, same 8-printer OrcaSlicer folder:\n\n| Import | Old code | New code |\n|---|---|---|\n| File › Import window | 50.7 s | 22.4 s |\n| First-launch step | 46 s | 21.5 s |\n\nThe menu pair ran back to back while another session's work had the machine fairly busy (load around 7 on 12 cores). The old first-launch number is from this afternoon.\n\n**One mistake along the way.** To build the old code for the timing comparison, I swapped in the old source files and then copied mine back with their original dates. The build tool took the old compiled code as current, so for a while the build folder held the old code. That doesn't affect the commits, and the earlier new-code timings used an app built before the swap. I've rebuilt from the new source, confirmed the app now contains the new code, and the native tests pass on it (166). The new commit's message also corrects the earlier one, which said the label showed on screen when I had only read it from the page.\n\n**Still open.** Most of the remaining time is OrcaSlicer saving each named printer, about 2.6 seconds each on a quiet machine. Each save copies the whole preset bundle for its compare dialog, and fixing that means changing OrcaSlicer's own code."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":333,"cache_read_input_tokens":349894,"output_tokens":695,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":333,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":695,"cache_read_input_tokens":349894,"cache_creation_input_tokens":333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":333},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgm7aEi9DmJrPeyGUKkJj","requestRef":"cff96574-b864-46b6-940e-18cebc63cb6b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"2efce90d-41ed-4c80-a770-8effa4359c77","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:22:20.619Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
