{"parentUuid":"4ddc28b2-e9e1-48c3-a098-48fff1bc080b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmAoKc2u4a3hPffbuTR5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The trial merge onto the updated jusprin-newui is clean, but another session has uncommitted changes in the main folder, including two files my commits also touch. I'm building the squashed commit on a new branch first so that folder stays untouched.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2074,"cache_read_input_tokens":352805,"output_tokens":2691,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1294},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2074,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2691,"cache_read_input_tokens":352805,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2074,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2074},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgmAoKJRFQdpiXuboM8h6","requestRef":"2e20192a-1dfc-402f-a302-946a93c25414","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"17232875-63f5-4d2e-afb0-1a24a007edac","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:04:46.102Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"17232875-63f5-4d2e-afb0-1a24a007edac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmAoKc2u4a3hPffbuTR5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RQwANyeh16Le3JBDKd9zWx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"T=$(git merge-tree --write-tree jusprin-newui HEAD) && echo tree $T && C=$(git commit-tree $T -p jusprin-newui -F - <<'EOF'\nFirst launch and File › Import: bring OrcaSlicer's printers in, now or later, with one profile reload\n\nFirst launch, Printers step:\n- \"Which printer do you have?\" is a screen of its own. A printer the\n  person skips shows as \"No printer yet\".\n- Importing from OrcaSlicer brings the printers OrcaSlicer has saved and\n  the ones its setup wizard ticked. Each saved printer's base profile is\n  installed first, so it imports instead of failing on a missing base.\n  Retry keeps the printer the first try selected.\n\nFile › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer… (new, after the first launch):\n- A window over the current screen finds OrcaSlicer's folder the same\n  way, lists its printers and marks the ones JusPrin already has as\n  \"Already in JusPrin\". A preset counts as already there when JusPrin has\n  one with the same name and the same base, compared as JusPrin loads\n  the base, so a second import brings nothing and saves no \"(Orca copy)\".\n- It leaves the open project's printer, filaments and process as they\n  were; imported printers only join the printer menu (Kenneth,\n  2026-11-05). Screens: found, imported (with Retry failed items),\n  nothing new, no folder, and a picked folder with no printers.\n- MainFrame.cpp (OrcaSlicer-owned) gets one additive append_menu_item\n  call in init_menubar_as_editor, in the import_menu block right after\n  \"Import Configs\". It calls JusPrin::installed_shell()->open_orca_import()\n  and is enabled only when the shell is installed. Carry it there at\n  each rebase.\n\nShared by both:\n- OrcaImporter does the detecting, importing, retrying and folder\n  picking for both. Every vendor, model and nozzle the import needs is\n  installed with one PresetBundle::apply_vendor_config\n  (SetupCommands::install_printer_profiles), which puts the previous\n  setup back if it fails; before, each printer reloaded every preset.\n- The printer list and result lines are one component,\n  AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImportLists.tsx, with its own stylesheet\n  and a guard test that it uses only variables both pages define.\n- Both pages show \"Importing…\" with the other buttons disabled and send\n  the request only after a second frame and 50 ms\n  (WebShared/afterPaint.ts). Sent sooner, the import blocked the UI\n  thread before it put the label on screen.\n\nTested: jusprin_tests (166 cases), AgentUI vitest (678), HomeUI vitest\n(155). In the built app with copies of an OrcaSlicer folder holding 8\nprinters, screen unlocked: the menu import took 22.4 s against 50.7 s\nfor the old code, back to back; the first-launch import took 21.5 s\nagainst 46 s. A second menu import showed \"nothing new\" with no\n\"(Orca copy)\" files, and the project's printer stayed \"Generic printer\".\nScreenshots taken during both imports showed \"Importing…\".\nEOF\n) && git branch claude/orca-import-squashed $C && git log --oneline -2 claude/orca-import-squashed && git diff --stat jusprin-newui claude/orca-import-squashed | tail -1 && git diff --stat a2d5550058 HEAD | tail -1 && git diff jusprin-newui claude/orca-import-squashed > /tmp/claude/sq.diff 2>/dev/null; git diff a2d5550058 HEAD | diff -q - <(git diff jusprin-newui claude/orca-import-squashed) && echo \"same change as the branch\"","description":"Build one squashed commit on top of jusprin-newui, on a new branch"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2074,"cache_read_input_tokens":352805,"output_tokens":2691,"output_tokens_details