{"parentUuid":"e027581d-b14a-4ca5-a152-e2b026f23140","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmAtVpLSrTYejcY4U4iB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I squashed my five commits into one, **34cc536134**, on top of the current `jusprin-newui`. It's on a new branch, `claude/orca-import-squashed`; `jusprin-newui` itself hasn't moved yet.\n\nThe five commits are the first-launch printer screen, the base-profile install, the File › Import window, the one-reload install with shared components, and the \"Importing…\" fix. The squashed commit makes exactly the same change as those five. `jusprin-newui` gained one commit since my branch started, 9e07257c2c (the printer chat's Done button), and it touches none of my files. On the combined code, both pages' tests and type checks pass (682 and 155 tests). That new commit changes no native code, so I didn't rerun the native tests.\n\n**Decision needed: how to put it on `jusprin-newui`.** You have `jusprin-newui` checked out in the main folder, `/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin`, with uncommitted changes in about 20 files from another session's work (credits and Preferences). Two of those files are ones my commit also changes: `AgentUI/src/styles.css` and `AgentUI/src/bridge/protocol.ts`. That means I can't land it from inside that folder without touching that work. The options:\n\n- **Wait until that folder's changes are committed (my pick).** Then I move `jusprin-newui` forward to my commit, or rebase my commit onto whatever was committed. It costs one more step later and puts nothing at risk.\n- **Move `jusprin-newui` to my commit now**, leaving the folder's files alone. Those files would no longer match the branch. In that folder, `git status` would list my whole change as staged to be undone, mixed in with the other session's work. A wrong commit there would revert my change.\n\nOne more thing to know: AGENTS.md, from your choice this morning, says to land branches with `git merge --no-ff`, never a squash. I followed your instruction here, so that rule doesn't match what you did this time. A side effect of the squash: `claude/first-run-printer-step` and `claude/orca-import-menu` will still look unmerged afterwards. They can be deleted once the squashed commit is on `jusprin-newui`.\n\nDo you want me to wait until that folder's changes are committed, or move `jusprin-newui` now?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":591,"cache_read_input_tokens":359475,"output_tokens":754,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":591,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":754,"cache_read_input_tokens":359475,"cache_creation_input_tokens":591,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":591},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgmAtVaCq8b9izHsUE5ej","requestRef":"61153369-bf85-48ee-b07c-81f1959fa76b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"fe15c718-373d-4751-a4df-bf8b288c29ef","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:05:49.225Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
