{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01Fx7UioApoHEkwHCUFqCo1e","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"7911d73c-5552-4877-a943-6a0eba3d7c4d","ownerOrganizationUuid":"68a648b0-98a4-49c7-902b-ff471f8d1d46"}
{"parentUuid":"fb596138-760b-486e-ad59-8c18394d5264","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmAzDSFYU7bYpZZTrov8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The design session sent a list of 23 changes to the first launch and asked me to make them all. It quotes you: \"tell the coding agent to fix all the issues you identified, based on your recommendations\". I haven't started, because the request came from another session rather than from you here, and it's a large piece of work.\n\nWhat the list covers:\n- **Welcome screen:** lead with \"Sign up free\", explain the choice in one line, and say what 500 credits buys in questions to the agent. The \"own API key\" and \"Claude Code\" options fold into one link.\n- **Signing in:** the email code comes first and the password box hides behind a link. Clearer wording on the code and Google screens.\n- **After signing in:** \"You got 500 free credits, good until 4 December\", using one name for those credits everywhere. The account card says \"Signed in as …\".\n- **OrcaSlicer import screen:** a tick box per printer, and a line naming the printer JusPrin will start with. \"Start fresh\" becomes \"Choose my printer instead\", and the filament count gets its own line.\n- **Printer step:**\n  - a \"Reading this printer's settings…\" spinner while a printer loads;\n  - the \"Choose the folder…\" link removed;\n  - honest wording for Skip, which installs a 250 mm Klipper printer, not a generic one.\n- **Home:** a printer with no connection set up gets a \"Connect it…\" hint in place of \"Not connected\", and the agent card says why to set it up.\n- **Import result:** the title stays \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\" when only some items fail. A clearer reason for a missing base profile. Retry only for failures a retry can fix. The \"OrcaSlicer's own files were not changed\" line goes.\n\nWhen I start, I'll work on top of the squashed commit 34cc536134, since most of these screens are in it. The tick boxes and the Retry rule get native tests, and each changed screen gets a screenshot. Before writing the credits line I'll look up the real cost per message.\n\nHow to land the squashed commit on `jusprin-newui` is still open. My pick is still to wait until the uncommitted changes in your main folder are committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1378,"cache_read_input_tokens":363776,"output_tokens":686,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1378,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":686,"cache_read_input_tokens":363776,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1378,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1378},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgmAzDBdH79TSEXubFXWD","requestRef":"e515fe99-f885-4a0d-b3ba-7efd115b6f73","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"6e9b42d8-3ff1-430b-b943-b45e1ee8a928","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:07:05.746Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
