{"parentUuid":"5bfa0c10-2401-44b0-8f7d-e629e37bc0d6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmBPYjkhrxWFrHgQF6wZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016hGnRtGVkXKPUe5kAXyjfi","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory && grep -l \"credits\" *.md | xargs grep -h -i \"expert.*5 credits\\|5 credits a message\\|Standard.*1 credit\\|credits\\\": *[0-9]\" | head -10; cat jusprin-cloud-provider.md | head -30","description":"Recall the deployed per-tier prices"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":504,"cache_read_input_tokens":140357,"output_tokens":242,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":42},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":504,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":242,"cache_read_input_tokens":140357,"cache_creation_input_tokens":504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":504},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016hGnRtGVkXKPUe5kAXyjfi":{"command":"cd ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory && grep -l \"credits\" *.md | xargs grep -h -i \"expert.*5 credits\\|5 credits a message\\|Standard.*1 credit\\|credits\\\": *[0-9]\" | head -10; cat jusprin-cloud-provider.md | head -30","description":"Recall the deployed per-tier prices"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgmBPYCWGxZksv54F8C4K","requestRef":"a9f56521-2379-4ab9-9482-9d45cbfb5a6d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"916905cb-3c45-4732-8869-ca5dc0978593","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:12:19.097Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/tsd-enterprise","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-fixes","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"916905cb-3c45-4732-8869-ca5dc0978593","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4e98f1e7-49ff-445f-823b-aeedc91e43e5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016hGnRtGVkXKPUe5kAXyjfi","type":"tool_result","content":"**How to apply:** no \"612 Standard or 112 Expert messages\" on any balance, offer or pricing card. Prices stay as \"5 credits a message\". The low-balance notice says \"About 25 credits left\", not \"About 5 Expert messages left\" (Kenneth, 2026-11-02: \"25 credits left\" directly, then \"About 25 credits left\" in his later keep list). Free credits get the same ring as any others, with no line of their own: \"No reason to make exception\". Canvas versions 73 and 74 applied this. The pricing session kept 5a's \"50 free Standard messages a month\", board 9's Workshop notices and 2c's caption, because they describe allowances or ceilings, not a balance. Related: [[credit-price-needs-its-unit]], [[usage-against-quota-common-shape]].\nKenneth on credits board 7a, 2026-11-02: \"keep the model /thinking selection design, but greyed out with a tooltip to explain that model can't be changed mid-chat. also explain the credits/msg\". So once a chat has a message, both pickers stay in place, greyed, and a tooltip gives the reason and the price (board 2c). This replaces my plain \"Expert · 5 credits a message\" text; the price per message is now in the menu and the tooltip.\n**How to apply:** wherever a price stands alone, say what it buys: \"Basic · 1 credit a message\", \"Expert · 5 credits a message\". The design doc's shorter strings are out of date. Related: [[usage-against-quota-common-shape]].\n**Pricing audit result:** the first-run branch touched only the onboarding screens, Home's agent group (reusing `balanceRows`) and Preferences' close-when-done; pickers, ring and panel, pre-send check, 402 card, low-balance notice, print-report form, the welcome-back window (boards 1c/1d) and the Preferences account row (1a) are untouched from the credits branch. One drift: the scale line under the offer reads \"Then paid, or your own key.\" and must be the decided \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\" Step 3 (Chargebee, Account and pricing pages, v1 carry-over) is unbuilt on both branches, and production's gateway lacks the ledger branch, which is why the account card showed no balance.\n---\nname: jusprin-cloud-provider\ndescription: \"JusPrin Cloud provider: LIVE IN PROD 2026-10-25 (obi.4048, app.obico.io); merged to tsd-enterprise/ops master and jusprin-newui; release recipe; domain question still open before the desktop app ships.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: db0d9105-2185-4020-918f-5caf79c71adb\n  modified: 2026-10-24T23:26:14.517Z\n---\n\nStarted 2026-10-24 from ~/Downloads/cloud-provider-plan.md plus decisions relayed from the plan-review session (they override the plan):\n- Alias \"slicer-1\" / \"Slicer 1\"; efforts \"fast\"/\"thorough\" map to low/high at the gateway. First upstream claude-sonnet-5-5.\n- Both formats: gateway passthrough /ent/jusprin/v2/messages (Anthropic) and /responses (OpenAI), no translation. GET /v2/models gives each alias's \"format\" for this person (server-side A/B by hash of user id). Each chat is pinned to the format of its first request (ChatModelChoice.format in the project doc); new chats take the current assignment.\n- New OAuth app client_id \"JusPrin2\" (public, authorization code, PKCE, redirect http://127.0.0.1/callback with no port; DOT 2.3 accepts any loopback port). Created by hand in admin like v1's \"JusPrin\" (README_jusprin_server.md), no migration.\n- v1 import on first launch: copy user/ + BambuNetworkEngine.conf + JusPrin.conf→JusPrin2.conf, v1 access_token becomes jusprin_agent/jusprin_api_key; welcome-back window from canvas boards V1-01..03. Kenneth will not rotate the dotenv.example key.\n\nWhere: client worktree `.claude/worktrees/jusprin-cloud-provider` (branch claude/jusprin-cloud-provider on d921c4b3dd, Release build dir); server worktree `~/Projects/tsd-enterprise-worktrees/jusprin-cloud` (claude/jusprin-cloud-gateway) with obico-server on claude/jusprin-v2-oauth-app. Pushed 2026-10-24 as one commit each: client branch `claude/jusprin-cloud-provider` (`ac55c2961a`, TheSpaghettiDetective/JusPrin), tsd-enterprise `claude/jusprin-cloud-gateway` (`3b54e5928f`, kennethjiang/tsd-enterprise; includes the large-request slots, shared upstream client, off-loop parse). obico-server has NO changes: Kenneth hasn't decided whether v2 is open-sourced, so the README commit was dropped and the compose change skipped. ops branch `claude/jusprin-v2-gateway-routing` handled by the ASGI side session. Staging is live at https://app-stg.obico.io; prod NOT rolled out.\n\n**Production rollout 2026-10-25 (Kenneth asked, without deciding the domain):** gateway 3b54e5928f merged to tsd-enterprise master; release branch df39c0dcfd (bundles copied from the previous release 76d9f2d602 because frontend/obico-server were unchanged) → CircleCI built `kennethjiang/web_ent:obi.4048`; staging and prod run it; prod Secret/ConfigMap `jusprin-v2-gateway-prod` (keys copied from the stg Secret), JusPrin2 OAuth app id 9 on prod (owner user 1), ingress rules on app.obico.io / app.thespaghettidetective.com / app.kingroon.com (kingroon's cert expired 2025-05-15, pre-existing). ops master 272cde9. Client merged to jusprin-newui as 889d28681c (pushed). No-model smoke script pattern: short-lived AccessToken for the JusPrin2 app owner, `unknown_model` bodies per format (the gateway rejects foreign fields first), delete the token. GCE was out of capacity for node scale-up in us-central1-c during the rollout; it still fit. Probing the stream paths before the URL map propagates (~2.5 min) creates a Sentry ImproperlyConfigured issue (1963, resolved).\n\n**Still open (Kenneth, 2026-10-24): whether JusPrin gets a dedicated domain instead of app.obico.io** — now: decide before the JusPrin 2 desktop app ships with that default. It moves the client's default gateway (ProviderProfile.hpp \"jusprin\" row), the OAuth sign-in pages and login cookies, the prod ingress rules and certificate, and imported v1 base_url values. Reminders sit in ProviderProfile.hpp, web_ent/jusprin/v2/urls.py and the ops RUNBOOK/prod draft.\n\nLocal server: compose project `jusprin-cloud` on port 3434 (Kenneth's own stack holds 3334), fake upstream `web_ent/scripts/jusprin/fake_upstream.py --port 8765`; test account in LOCAL_TEST_ACCOUNT.txt. The session cookie is scoped to \".localhost\", so a Python cookie jar won't send it back to localhost: pass it as a header.\n\n**Prod topology finding:** tsdweb-prod is gunicorn sync workers; only tsdws-prod runs daphne (`config.asgi:application`). The gateway's two streaming paths are a raw ASGI endpoint (Django 4.0 can't stream async) behind a router set as ASGI_APPLICATION, so prod needs an ingress rule sending them to tsdws-prod. Kenneth wants a simple single-Django-project topology; decision pending. Compose files that start daphne with `config.routing:application` bypass the router.\n\n**End-to-end run, 2026-10-24 (all passed after one fix):** v1 import → welcome window (V1-02 with real data, V1-03 with a revoked token) → chat through /v2/responses → server switched to anthropic → old chat stayed on /responses, new chat went to /messages → in-app browser sign-in via OrcaSlicer's loopback 41172 → sign-out revoked the token (200 → 401). The run found that /jusprin/api/me/ nests the email under \"user\" (fixed). Tooling in `~/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/cloud-e2e/` (instrumented page server, browser stand-in that logs in with the test account, fake v1 builder, run.sh).\n\nTraps from that run: hook `window.__jusprinBridge` with a defineProperty setter, or a polling hook misses the handshake and the window looks silent; serve the instrumented page with Cache-Control: no-store (WKWebView reuses the previous run's page); a v1 settings file (version 1.4.0) makes Orca show its modal \"Profile syncing change\" notice at start-up, which posted keys can't dismiss but an AppleScript click on its AXCloseButton can; a fixture v1 settings file needs the `models` list or no system profiles load and every imported preset looks orphaned.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5e603786-414e-41dc-b7b7-d5ad51517da4","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:12:19.299Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"**How to apply:** no \"612 Standard or 112 Expert messages\" on any balance, offer or pricing card. Prices stay as \"5 credits a message\". The low-balance notice says \"About 25 credits left\", not \"About 5 Expert messages left\" (Kenneth, 2026-11-02: \"25 credits left\" directly, then \"About 25 credits left\" in his later keep list). Free credits get the same ring as any others, with no line of their own: \"No reason to make exception\". Canvas versions 73 and 74 applied this. The pricing session kept 5a's \"50 free Standard messages a month\", board 9's Workshop notices and 2c's caption, because they describe allowances or ceilings, not a balance. Related: [[credit-price-needs-its-unit]], [[usage-against-quota-common-shape]].\nKenneth on credits board 7a, 2026-11-02: \"keep the model /thinking selection design, but greyed out with a tooltip to explain that model can't be changed mid-chat. also explain the credits/msg\". So once a chat has a message, both pickers stay in place, greyed, and a tooltip gives the reason and the price (board 2c). This replaces my plain \"Expert · 5 credits a message\" text; the price per message is now in the menu and the tooltip.\n**How to apply:** wherever a price stands alone, say what it buys: \"Basic · 1 credit a message\", \"Expert · 5 credits a message\". The design doc's shorter strings are out of date. Related: [[usage-against-quota-common-shape]].\n**Pricing audit result:** the first-run branch touched only the onboarding screens, Home's agent group (reusing `balanceRows`) and Preferences' close-when-done; pickers, ring and panel, pre-send check, 402 card, low-balance notice, print-report form, the welcome-back window (boards 1c/1d) and the Preferences account row (1a) are untouched from the credits branch. One drift: the scale line under the offer reads \"Then paid, or your own key.\" and must be the decided \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\" Step 3 (Chargebee, Account and pricing pages, v1 carry-over) is unbuilt on both branches, and production's gateway lacks the ledger branch, which is why the account card showed no balance.\n---\nname: jusprin-cloud-provider\ndescription: \"JusPrin Cloud provider: LIVE IN PROD 2026-10-25 (obi.4048, app.obico.io); merged to tsd-enterprise/ops master and jusprin-newui; release recipe; domain question still open before the desktop app ships.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: db0d9105-2185-4020-918f-5caf79c71adb\n  modified: 2026-10-24T23:26:14.517Z\n---\n\nStarted 2026-10-24 from ~/Downloads/cloud-provider-plan.md plus decisions relayed from the plan-review session (they override the plan):\n- Alias \"slicer-1\" / \"Slicer 1\"; efforts \"fast\"/\"thorough\" map to low/high at the gateway. First upstream claude-sonnet-5-5.\n- Both formats: gateway passthrough /ent/jusprin/v2/messages (Anthropic) and /responses (OpenAI), no translation. GET /v2/models gives each alias's \"format\" for this person (server-side A/B by hash of user id). Each chat is pinned to the format of its first request (ChatModelChoice.format in the project doc); new chats take the current assignment.\n- New OAuth app client_id \"JusPrin2\" (public, authorization code, PKCE, redirect http://127.0.0.1/callback with no port; DOT 2.3 accepts any loopback port). Created by hand in admin like v1's \"JusPrin\" (README_jusprin_server.md), no migration.\n- v1 import on first launch: copy user/ + BambuNetworkEngine.conf + JusPrin.conf→JusPrin2.conf, v1 access_token becomes jusp