{"parentUuid":"4f5f4930-46c3-45c9-a716-906495d021c3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmDKNMYtiPFpi7RyfBeX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017bc4ZvFyRJUvxZdtTLm56Z","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35; git add resources/jusprin/home/protocol.json src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin tests/jusprin && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nFirst launch: clearer sign-up offer, email code first, tick boxes for OrcaSlicer's printers, Retry only when it can help\n\nSign-up and the welcome\n- The offer reads \"Sign up and get 500 free credits\", says they last the\n  first month and come to about 100 messages on Expert, and the email\n  button reads \"Sign up free\" with an \"Already have an account? Sign in\"\n  link beside it.\n- The email door asks for a code first; \"Use a password instead\" reveals\n  the password row. The code step says the email can be opened on a phone.\n- After signing in, the welcome and the printer step lead with the credits\n  (\"You got 500 free credits for signing up, good until 5 December.\"), then\n  \"Signed in as ...\".\n- \"Use your own AI account instead\" replaces the two free-door cards. The\n  browser wait reads \"Finish in your browser.\"\n\nPrinters\n- The OrcaSlicer import screen ticks every printer at first and imports only\n  the ticked ones (orca_import_chosen), with every filament and process. It\n  says which printer JusPrin starts with. \"Choose the folder...\" is gone from\n  the first launch; File > Import keeps it.\n- File > Import > Import from OrcaSlicer... has the same tick boxes.\n- The import result lists each failure with its reason as a sentence, and\n  shows Retry only when some failure can be fixed by retrying\n  (orca_import_retryable: an unreadable file, or a preset JusPrin couldn't\n  load).\n- The printer step shows \"Reading this printer's settings...\" while a model\n  loads, and every no-printer line says files are sliced for a 250 mm\n  Klipper printer until the person adds theirs.\n- A printer card with no connection ever set up hides the status row and\n  says \"Connect it to send prints straight from JusPrin\" beside Connect.\n\nTests: C++ cases for the chosen-printer filter and for when Retry shows;\nHomeUI and AgentUI tests updated.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1; git status --short","description":"Commit the first-launch fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":188260,"output_tokens":880,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":342,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":880,"cache_read_input_tokens":188260,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":342},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017bc4ZvFyRJUvxZdtTLm56Z":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35; git add resources/jusprin/home/protocol.json src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin tests/jusprin && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nFirst launch: clearer sign-up offer, email code first, tick boxes for OrcaSlicer's printers, Retry only when it can help\n\nSign-up and the welcome\n- The offer reads \"Sign up and get 500 free credits\", says they last the\n  first month and come to about 100 messages on Expert, and the email\n  button reads \"Sign up free\" with an \"Already have an account? Sign in\"\n  link beside it.\n- The email door asks for a code first; \"Use a password instead\" reveals\n  the password row. The code step says the email can be opened on a phone.\n- After signing in, the welcome and the printer step lead with the credits\n  (\"You got 500 free credits for signing up, good until 5 December.\"), then\n  \"Signed in as ...\".\n- \"Use your own AI account instead\" replaces the two free-door cards. The\n  browser wait reads \"Finish in your browser.\"\n\nPrinters\n- The OrcaSlicer import screen ticks every printer at first and imports only\n  the ticked ones (orca_import_chosen), with every filament and process. It\n  says which printer JusPrin starts with. \"Choose the folder...\" is gone from\n  the first launch; File > Import keeps it.\n- File > Import > Import from OrcaSlicer... has the same tick boxes.\n- The import result lists each failure with its reason as a sentence, and\n  shows Retry only when some failure can be fixed by retrying\n  (orca_import_retryable: an unreadable file, or a preset JusPrin couldn't\n  load).\n- The printer step shows \"Reading this printer's settings...\" while a model\n  loads, and every no-printer line says files are sliced for a 250 mm\n  Klipper printer until the person adds theirs.\n- A printer card with no connection ever set up hides the status row and\n  says \"Connect it to send prints straight from JusPrin\" beside Connect.\n\nTests: C++ cases for the chosen-printer filter and for when Retry shows;\nHomeUI and AgentUI tests updated.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1; git status --short","description":"Commit the first-launch fixes"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgmDKMw1A5xkX1oBLHiEL","requestRef":"84e1e7fa-4d79-43aa-aa5a-1c4e62e41311","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"167ed3a1-6daf-4bd0-84aa-dbc769ee37a2","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:37:40.806Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-