{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","id":"5415cfef-7fa5-4e93-8a2b-5f1b166e8650","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:38:03.623Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"6be4cbcf13bd24f91c1084271e54c66443d4511e9a00e5bc8042b89ce33d2e34","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"4a7c2551-d808-47f5-95df-256d650f9c32","keep":203,"tail":["eb9cdb23b6d08cb13b662b7c731801bb7ca3b5bb41207f4cbbadf723fd82f11a","d80a17f62c7f0f80e5373df47936236d76cffcbcf40e8ac8463e27eca5231842","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",205,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"117a65217655b5c79687be9d9c1074ccd996e5f8fdcd457b771a66b6b75fefc2"}
{"parentUuid":"1d60f61c-e15a-428a-90b9-8e0b6fa3f910","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmDMfXiWb9szuCJb9rPU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I committed all 23 first-launch fixes as 076042104d on `claude/first-run-fixes`, on top of 34cc536134. The C++, Home page and Agent page tests pass, including `wording.test.ts`. I walked the changed screens in a scratch copy of the app and saved 17 screenshots. Nothing is pushed or merged.\n\n**Tests:**\n- C++: 169 cases, 1,036 checks. Two are new:\n  - only the ticked printers are imported, along with every filament and process;\n  - Retry shows only when a retry can fix the failure: a file that couldn't be read, or a preset JusPrin couldn't load.\n- Home page: 155 tests. Agent page: 682 tests.\n\n**What I saw in the app:**\n- **Signed out:** the welcome now offers 500 free credits for the first month, \"about 100 messages to the agent on Expert\". The email door shows only \"Email me a 6-digit code\"; \"Use a password instead\" reveals the password row.\n- **OrcaSlicer import:** every printer starts ticked. Unticking the P1S, which OrcaSlicer had selected, changed the line to \"JusPrin starts with Creality Ender-3 V2 Neo…\".\n- **Choose my printer instead:** this leads to the printer step, where the spinner \"Reading this printer's settings…\" showed while the P1S profile loaded. That was a real load, not an injected state.\n- **Skip:** Home shows the 250 mm Klipper line in the drop zone and on the \"No printer yet\" card, plus a \"Set up the agent\" card offering 500 credits.\n- **Signed in:** the welcome leads with \"You got 500 free credits for signing up, good until 5 December\", then \"Signed in as …\". I unticked two printers and imported the rest:\n  - Only the other six printers came in.\n  - The half-written filament showed \"Not imported. The file couldn't be read.\" and Retry appeared.\n  - On Home, printers with no connection show \"Connect it to send prints straight from JusPrin\" in place of a status. The one with an Obico connection still shows \"Connected\".\n- **File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer…:** lists the two printers I'd unticked, both ticked, with the button \"Import 2 printers\".\n\n**Not checked in the app:**\n- The \"type the code\" step and the \"Finish in your browser\" card. I injected those states into the page so no real email went out.\n- Unticking a printer in the File › Import window and importing. The screen-control tool refused clicks inside that window's web page, and I didn't work around it. The unit tests cover it.\n\n**Open, not part of this work:** after an import, the drop zone said \"plans the print for your Anycubic Kobra 3\", but JusPrin had selected the P1S. That line names whichever printer card comes first alphabetically. The code predates this branch. I left it alone and can fix it separately.\n\nThe screenshots are in `/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_4d17825a-ac19-4732-a080-7e0c1dca6d1c/first-run-fixes-shots/`.\n\n**Decision needed:** how should 34cc536134 and this commit land on jusprin-newui? The project rules say to land a branch with a `--no-ff` merge, never a squash. The main checkout has someone's uncommitted work, so merging there now could tangle with it. Moving the branch from this worktree is possible, but the main checkout's files would then lag behind its own branch. My pick is to wait until the main checkout is clean, then merge `claude/first-run-fixes` with one `--no-ff` merge. Should I wait, or merge now?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":656,"cache_read_input_tokens":191197,"output_tokens":1195,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":656,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1195,"cache_read_input_tokens":191197,"cache_creation_input_tokens":656,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":656},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgmDMfFqnLcRvaGHDv2sL","requestRef":"5415cfef-7fa5-4e93-8a2b-5f1b166e8650","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"5583beb0-7bf0-4731-999f-0aa1dfb2265b","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:38:16.083Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-fixes","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
