e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8370c395-02d1-43e7-af4d-f3f533844160","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:09:16.253Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-fixes","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"8370c395-02d1-43e7-af4d-f3f533844160","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6c0ca605-5f81-42cd-84fe-0bb18d7f5bdc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014czx2UePUmv9N4wM9mNd6m","type":"tool_result","content":"88:## Landing a branch on jusprin-newui\n89-\n90-- Merge a feature branch with `git merge --no-ff`, never a squash. Make the merge message one line saying what the branch delivers: `Merge claude/<branch>: <what it delivers>`.\n91-- Read the history one line per feature with `git log --first-parent jusprin-newui`.\n92-- Why: a squash drops the step commits that `git blame` and `git bisect` need. It also leaves every branch the squashed one had merged looking unmerged, so the same work gets merged again with conflicts. Kenneth chose this on 2026-11-05.\n93-\n94-## Critical Constraints\na2d5550058 2026-11-05 12:40:57 -0800 Kenneth Jiang Land feature branches on jusprin-newui with --no-ff merges, not squashes\n---\nname: merge-no-ff-not-squash\ndescription: \"2026-11-05: Kenneth chose --no-ff merges, not squashes, for landing feature branches on jusprin-newui; the rule is in AGENTS.md (a2d5550058).\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983\n  modified: 2026-11-05T20:41:38.743Z\n---\n\nLand a feature branch on jusprin-newui with `git merge --no-ff` and a one-line message `Merge claude/<branch>: <what it delivers>`; read the history with `git log --first-parent`. Kenneth asked whether to squash for a clean log; I recommended --no-ff and he said \"Okay, go with what you suggested.\" Written into AGENTS.md as \"Landing a branch on jusprin-newui\" (commit a2d5550058).\n\n**Why:** the sign-in branch was squashed into f46e5ac05f (117 files, 19 commits). That lost the step history for blame/bisect, and left origin/credits-integration-2026-11 showing 16 \"unmerged\" commits whose content was already in. That branch and local claude/credits-onboarding were deleted; the steps survive on origin/claude/elated-sutherland-84a741.\n\n**How to apply:** don't squash an existing pushed squash back out (rewriting jusprin-newui is worse). Before landing, check the branch doesn't drag in another branch that will be merged separately.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4ce0a612-331a-4b2b-b903-8638a82daed9","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:09:16.631Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"88:## Landing a branch on jusprin-newui\n89-\n90-- Merge a feature branch with `git merge --no-ff`, never a squash. Make the merge message one line saying what the branch delivers: `Merge claude/<branch>: <what it delivers>`.\n91-- Read the history one line per feature with `git log --first-parent jusprin-newui`.\n92-- Why: a squash drops the step commits that `git blame` and `git bisect` need. It also leaves every branch the squashed one had merged looking unmerged, so the same work gets merged again with conflicts. Kenneth chose this on 2026-11-05.\n93-\n94-## Critical Constraints\na2d5550058 2026-11-05 12:40:57 -0800 Kenneth Jiang Land feature branches on jusprin-newui with --no-ff merges, not squashes\n---\nname: merge-no-ff-not-squash\ndescription: \"2026-11-05: Kenneth chose --no-ff merges, not squashes, for landing feature branches on jusprin-newui; the rule is in AGENTS.md (a2d5550058).\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983\n  modified: 2026-11-05T20:41:38.743Z\n---\n\nLand a feature branch on jusprin-newui with `git merge --no-ff` and a one-line message `Merge claude/<branch>: <what it delivers>`; read the history with `git log --first-parent`. Kenneth asked whether to squash for a clean log; I recommended --no-ff and he said \"Okay, go with what you suggested.\" Written into AGENTS.md as \"Landing a branch on jusprin-newui\" (commit a2d5550058).\n\n**Why:** the sign-in branch was squashed into f46e5ac05f (117 files, 19 commits). That lost the step history for blame/bisect, and left origin/credits-integration-2026-11 showing 16 \"unmerged\" commits whose content was already in. That branch and local claude/credits-onboarding were deleted; the steps survive on origin/claude/elated-sutherland-84a741.\n\n**How to apply:** don't squash an existing pushed squash back out (rewriting jusprin-newui is worse). Before landing, check the branch doesn't drag in another branch that will be merged separately.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8370c395-02d1-43e7-af4d-f3f533844160","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-fixes","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
