 not squashes, for landing feature branches on jusprin-newui; the rule is in AGENTS.md (a2d5550058).\"","+description: \"2026-11-06: Kenneth removed the AGENTS.md rule 'land feature branches on jusprin-newui with --no-ff, never squash' (removal commit 96c7bda756). No standing rule; ask how to land.\""," metadata:","   node_type: memory","   type: feedback","   originSessionId: c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","-  modified: 2026-11-05T20:41:38.743Z","+  modified: 2026-11-06T13:12:56.743Z"," ---"," ","-Land a feature branch on jusprin-newui with `git merge --no-ff` and a one-line message `Merge claude/<branch>: <what it delivers>`; read the history with `git log --first-parent`. Kenneth asked whether to squash for a clean log; I recommended --no-ff and he said \"Okay, go with what you suggested.\" Written into AGENTS.md as \"Landing a branch on jusprin-newui\" (commit a2d5550058).","+On 2026-11-05 Kenneth asked whether to squash for a clean log; I recommended `git merge --no-ff` and he said \"Okay, go with what you suggested.\" I wrote that into AGENTS.md as \"Landing a branch on jusprin-newui\" (a2d5550058), in my own words, and later called it \"the project rules\" to him."," ","-**Why:** the sign-in branch was squashed into f46e5ac05f (117 files, 19 commits). That lost the step history for blame/bisect, and left origin/credits-integration-2026-11 showing 16 \"unmerged\" commits whose content was already in. That branch and local claude/credits-onboarding were deleted; the steps survive on origin/claude/elated-sutherland-84a741.","+On 2026-11-06 he asked where the rule said that, then asked to remove it. Removed in 96c7bda756 on claude/first-run-fixes (reaches jusprin-newui only when that branch lands)."," ","-**How to apply:** don't squash an existing pushed squash back out (rewriting jusprin-newui is worse). Before landing, check the branch doesn't drag in another branch that will be merged separately.","+**Why:** the rule text was mine, not his; he had agreed to one recommendation, not to a standing rule. See [[trace-a-rule-to-kenneths-words]].","+","+**How to apply:** don't cite --no-ff-only as a project rule. When landing a branch, ask Kenneth how he wants it landed (merge or squash) unless he has said so for that branch."]}],"originalFile":"---\nname: merge-no-ff-not-squash\ndescription: \"2026-11-05: Kenneth chose --no-ff merges, not squashes, for landing feature branches on jusprin-newui; the rule is in AGENTS.md (a2d5550058).\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983\n  modified: 2026-11-05T20:41:38.743Z\n---\n\nLand a feature branch on jusprin-newui with `git merge --no-ff` and a one-line message `Merge claude/<branch>: <what it delivers>`; read the history with `git log --first-parent`. Kenneth asked whether to squash for a clean log; I recommended --no-ff and he said \"Okay, go with what you suggested.\" Written into AGENTS.md as \"Landing a branch on jusprin-newui\" (commit a2d5550058).\n\n**Why:** the sign-in branch was squashed into f46e5ac05f (117 files, 19 commits). That lost the step history for blame/bisect, and left origin/credits-integration-2026-11 showing 16 \"unmerged\" commits whose content was already in. That branch and local claude/credits-onboarding were deleted; the steps survive on origin/claude/elated-sutherland-84a741.\n\n**How to apply:** don't squash an existing pushed squash back out (rewriting jusprin-newui is worse). Before landing, check the branch doesn't drag in another branch that will be merged separately.\n","userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"35f613ae-5cc7-4964-a333-43206f4d10b0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-fixes","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
