{"parentUuid":"94070cdd-2d25-4016-ab4f-6457f1c250d7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmjUUYrA9UbsLnLtwAcv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I removed the rule from `AGENTS.md` in commit 96c7bda756 on `claude/first-run-fixes`. I took out the whole \"Landing a branch on jusprin-newui\" section, not just the one line. The section's other two lines only made sense with that line: one says to read history with `--first-parent`, the other gives the reason for the rule. If you want those two kept, I'll put them back.\n\njusprin-newui still has the rule. That branch now ends at ed9776644e (\"Preferences › Account: show the account's credits and usage\"), which another session pushed. The removal reaches jusprin-newui only when `claude/first-run-fixes` lands. I also updated my memory so later sessions don't call it a project rule, and ask you how to land a branch instead.\n\n**Commits this session made, oldest first** (dates are your local time):\n\nJusPrin, the email and Google sign-in work (later squashed into f46e5ac05f by another session):\n- 3df2ed9c24, 11-03: Send each email sign-in step to the Home page\n- 4f44bffae5, 11-03: Sign in by email through allauth's app API, choosing a code or the password\n- ae1b916bbe, 11-03: Fit the sign-in door into Home's narrow agent card\n\ntsd-enterprise and its obico-server submodule (the server side of sign-in):\n- aa70569e4f, 11-03: Build JusPrin's email sign-in on allauth and django-oauth-toolkit\n- d799b57e37, 11-03: Drop the test for two accounts sharing an address in one syndicate\n- 17e87ee16e, 11-03: Serve JusPrin's email sign-in from allauth's API for apps\n- 731f6947 (obico-server), 11-03: Look accounts up by email the same way everywhere, within one syndicate\n- 5daee67e1b, 11-03: Start accounts made by signing in to JusPrin 2 on Obico's free plan\n- cf01e7adbf, 11-03: the revert of 5daee67e1b\n\nops (staging releases):\n- d54186e, 11-03: Release obi.4060 to staging only\n- 564b789, 11-03: Release obi.4063 to staging only\n- c27f5c8, 11-03: Roll staging back to obi.4060, without the JusPrin trial skip\n\nJusPrin, 11-05 and 11-06:\n- a2d5550058: Land feature branches on jusprin-newui with --no-ff merges, not squashes. This is the rule you just had removed.\n- 51aae77401: Keep OrcaSlicer's cloud login in its encrypted file, not the macOS keychain (branch `claude/encrypted-token-file`)\n- 3975401b9d: First launch: ask which printer on a screen of its own\n- d606562b06: OrcaSlicer import: install each saved printer's base profile first\n- ee3a17e64b: File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer\n- 242a9e73ba: OrcaSlicer import: install every needed profile in one reload\n- 37c24299b9: OrcaSlicer import: wait a second frame so \"Importing…\" shows\n- 34cc536134: the five commits above squashed into one, at your request (branch `claude/orca-import-squashed`)\n- 076042104d: the 23 first-launch fixes (branch `claude/first-run-fixes`)\n- 96c7bda756: the rule removal\n\nOf these, a2d5550058 is on jusprin-newui and pushed. The JusPrin commits from 11-03 reached jusprin-newui inside f46e5ac05f. The tsd-enterprise and ops commits went to those repos' own branches, and I pushed some of them at the time. The rest of the JusPrin commits are on local branches only, not pushed or merged.\n\nTwo commits near these in the log are not mine: 9e07257c2c (Printer chat Done button) and d354a20687 (Announce a project open's result)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":214,"cache_read_input_tokens":224650,"output_tokens":1296,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":214,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1296,"cache_read_input_